- Decision entry written; `01-architecture.md`, `12-client-engine.md` (all PORT tasks `[x]`), AGENTS.md, `directory.md`, README.md match the code.', '2026-10-12T03:26:41Z', 60);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (52, 4, 'Audit report media.py licenses', 700, 'Part 2 of milestone 4 (PUB-1): a report over every picked media file in the source pool that says which files must be replaced before a public release, and why. It reads only the licence record that plan 26 stored per slot (`provider`, `license`, `license_url`, `author`, `author_url`, `restrictions`, `pd_reasons`); no network at report time. The classification is one function that the review tool (plan of part 3, task 109) and `qgen validate` reuse, so the three never disagree.

## Classification: `providers.licence_verdict(slot)`
- In `authoring/tools/providers/__init__.py`, next to `licence_kind` and `LICENCE_FIELDS`; returns `("ok" | "replace", [reasons])`, reasons as short codes plus text (e.g. `off-allowlist: GFDL 1.2`).
- `replace` when any of:
  - **missing data:** a field of `LICENCE_FIELDS` absent, `restrictions`/`pd_reasons` not a list, unknown `provider` (same test as `qgen.licence_problem`, which then calls this function instead of its own check).
  - **off the allowlist:** `licence_kind(license)` is None (GFDL, GPL, NC, ND, unknown; D-45).
  - **PD without a reason:** family `public-domain` and `pd_reasons == []` (none today).
  - **PD-US only:** family `public-domain` and every reason is US-only. US-only = a constant list of patterns, e.g. `PD-US*` (not `PD-USGov*`), `PD-1923`, `PD-Harris-Ewing`; any other reason (`PD-old-*`, `PD-self`, `PD-author`, `PD-Art`, `PD-textlogo`, …) makes the file worldwide-ok. `PD-old-70-1923` style combined templates count as worldwide.
  - `PD-USGov*` (NASA, NPS, …, ~55 files) counts as ok, as in `plans/17-publishing.md` (US government works, generally treated as free elsewhere); write this choice down as a D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` with the US-only list.
- **Never** `replace` for `restrictions` (personality, trademarked, design, insignia, fan-art): listed for information only (D-61, decision 8).
- State of the pool on 2026-10-11 for a sanity check: 1,146 distinct files; off allowlist 1 (GFDL 1.2, q-0021, needs_work); PD-US only 2 (q-1100 `PD-US-not renewed`, q-1194 `PD-Harris-Ewing` + `PD-US-no notice`); 26 restriction flags.

## Report: `trivia-media licenses`
- New subcommand in `authoring/tools/media.py` (`cmd_licenses`), reading `authoring/data/questions.json` (all bundles, both slots `media` and `background`).
- One row per distinct file (`file_url`); a file used by several questions/slots is one row with all of them.
- Row: verdict, reasons, licence, family (`licence_kind`), PD reasons, restrictions, provider, `source_url`, question ids with slot and status.
- Questions with status `rejected` are left out (their picks never ship); `draft`, `needs_work`, `approved` count, so q-0021 (needs_work) stays on the list until part 3 replaces it.
- Output, in this order:
  1. **Replacement list:** the `replace` rows, grouped by reason, each with question ids, status and `source_url`. Ends with `nothing to replace` when empty (the milestone''s "done when").
  2. **Restriction flags:** the flagged files, per code, for information.
  3. **Tally:** files per licence family and per licence name, like the table in `plans/17-publishing.md` ("Media licenses"), plus PD reasons grouped (worldwide / US government / US only).
- Flags: `--status approved` (only that status), `--json` (rows as JSON, for scripts and part 3).
- Exit code 1 when the replacement list isn''t empty, so a script can gate on it; 0 otherwise.
- Help text in the module docstring; the command line in `AGENTS.md` ("Commands", Media line) and `README.md` if it lists `trivia-media` commands.

## Reuse by later parts
- `qgen validate` (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`, `licence_problem`): builds on `licence_verdict` for the missing-data and allowlist errors it already has. The new PD-US-only verdict becomes an error on approved questions only with part 3''s optional gate, not here (q-1100, q-1194 are approved and must not break `validate` before the gamemaster replaced them).
- Review tool (part 3, task 109): calls `licence_verdict` per slot for the `/review?licence=replace` filter and the reason next to the slot; nothing review-specific in this plan.

## Docs
- `plans/17-publishing.md`: PUB-1 `[x]` with a note (date, counts of the first run); refresh the tally table from the report''s output.
- `plans/23-media-providers.md`: the line "`PD-US`-only files are still a PUB-1 question" points to the verdict.

## How to check it worked
- `trivia-media licenses` lists exactly q-0021 (GFDL), q-1100 and q-1194 (PD-US only) today, lists the 26 restriction flags without classifying them, and exits 1.
- A throw-away script: a slot without `pd_reasons`, a `Public domain` slot with `[]`, one with `["PD-USGov-NASA"]`, one with `["PD-old-70-1923"]`, one with `["PD-US-expired"]`, a `CC BY-SA 4.0` slot with `["personality"]` → replace, replace, ok, ok, replace, ok.
- `qgen validate` reports the same errors as before the change.', '2026-10-12T03:29:53Z', 108);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (53, 4, 'Replace problem licence files in the review tool', 400, 'Part 3 of milestone 4 (PUB-3): the gamemaster replaces every media file that the audit (plan 52) puts on the replacement list, in the review tool, by hand. Runs after plan 26 (licence fields per slot, done) and plan 52 (`providers.licence_verdict(slot)`, `trivia-media licenses`); it adds no classification of its own, so review tool, report and `qgen validate` never disagree. Expected list on 2026-10-11: q-0021 (GFDL 1.2, needs_work), q-1100 and q-1194 (PD-US only, approved).

## Rules
- The gamemaster picks; no LLM pick, no automatic swap, no batch command that replaces files (milestone constraint).
- Restriction flags are never a reason to replace and get no "checked, keep" mark (D-61, decision 8): the review tool shows them as info at most.
- A new pick goes through `media.download` → `media.pick_fields`, so it gets plan 26''s licence fields like any pick; nothing new to store.
- Rejected questions are not on the list (plan 52); the filter follows the same rule.

## Server (`authoring/server/main.py`)
- Every question in API responses carries `licence`: per picked slot (`media`, `background`) `{"verdict": "ok"|"replace", "reasons": [...]}` from `providers.licence_verdict`; unpicked slots left out. Added in `with_candidates` (rename if it no longer fits).
- `GET /api/questions?licence=replace`: questions (not `rejected`) with at least one slot whose verdict is `replace`; combines with the other filters. Docstring API list updated.
- Search over all providers for a replacement: `media.find_candidates` stops asking the next provider once it has `ENOUGH`; `POST …/media/search` gets an optional `"all": true` that asks every available provider (`providers.order`) and keeps up to `MAX_CANDIDATES`. Param on `find_candidates`/`fetch_for`, default unchanged, so `qgen batch` behaves as before.
- After a pick the response carries the new verdict; a pick that is itself `replace` (e.g. another PD-US-only file; PD reasons are only known at pick time) is allowed and stays on the list, the UI shows why.
- `overview.build`: count of questions on the list, for a start-page link (only when > 0).

## UI (`authoring/ui/`)
- `lib/types.ts`, `lib/api.ts`: `licence` on `Question`, `licence` in `QuestionFilter`, `all` on the search call.
- `review/Review.svelte`: `licence=replace` read from the URL like `media=missing`; `filterText` says "licence to replace"; `isOpen` in this queue = some slot still `replace` (a question leaves the queue only with a clean pick, whoever reviewed it), so the queue walks the list once and the summary says when it is empty.
- `review/MediaPanel.svelte`: next to the slot''s credit, the reasons when the verdict is `replace` (e.g. "replace: PD-US only (PD-US-not renewed)"), plus licence, PD reasons and restrictions as small info text; the existing candidate list and `m` search modal do the replacing; in this queue the search uses `all: true`.
- `home/Home.svelte`: "Licences to replace (N)" link to `/review?licence=replace` when N > 0.
- Picking does not change the review status: q-0021 stays needs_work until the gamemaster approves it after the new pick; q-1100/q-1194 stay approved.

## Human pass
- The gamemaster opens `/review?licence=replace`, picks a new file per slot (candidates or new search), until the queue is empty and `trivia-media licenses` prints `nothing to replace` (exit 0).
- Then `trivia-media sync --status approved --prune` drops the old files from the cache (D-17).
- In pm: the gate task checks the list first; if it isn''t empty it raises a decision "Replace the files on the licence list" (one option: "done") and waits on it.

## Gate (optional part of the milestone, done here)
- `qgen validate`: an approved question with a slot whose `licence_verdict` is `replace` is an error (reasons in the message), so a replaced file can''t come back. Only after the list is empty, or validate breaks.
- `qgen batch` media step (`qgen.py`, where `media_tool.pick_fields(found[n - 1], slot)` is called): when the LLM''s pick comes back `replace`, the question gets needs_work with problem `media` and a short Spanish feedback like the "no adecuada" ones, never an approved question with a bad file.

## Docs
- `plans/17-publishing.md`: PUB-3 `[x]` with date and the replaced files; tally refreshed from `trivia-media licenses`.
- `plans/08-review-tool.md`: the `licence=replace` queue and the `all` search; `AGENTS.md` "Commands": `/review?licence=replace` in the authoring line.
- Milestone 4 "done when": `qgen validate` requires licence data (plan 26) and the list is empty; note both in the gate task''s done note.

## How to check it worked
- `/api/questions?licence=replace` returns q-0021, q-1100, q-1194 before the pass, `[]` after; ids match `trivia-media licenses --json`.
- Throw-away script: a pick via the API on a test copy of the pool gets all `LICENCE_FIELDS` and a verdict in the response.
- `npm run check`, `npm run build`; the queue in the browser shows the reasons and empties as picks are made.
- After the gate: `qgen validate` passes; a hand-edited approved slot with `pd_reasons: ["PD-US-expired"]` (throw-away copy) makes it fail.', '2026-10-12T03:31:08Z', 109);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (54, 8, 'Desktop shell skeleton (SW-2)', 480, 'An Electron window (D-63) that plays the built client from `app/client/dist/` with no Python process: fullscreen by default, F11 toggles, a minimal preload bridge, and a custom `app://` protocol that answers the client''s URLs (`/data/…`, `/media?url=…`, fonts, audio) from files. Dev on NixOS through the flake''s Electron and a `trivia-desktop` command. Part 1 of masterplan 8 (S3); owner `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-2). Saves stay in memory here; the save file is part 2 (SW-3, task 210), the builds part 3 (SW-5/6, task 211).

## Depends on
- D-63 / pm decision 12: Electron. Steam binding picked here (task 4), not added (S5, SW-8).
- Plan 50 (PORT-7): `/data/…` URLs and `lib/data.ts` (task 297); screens on the engine, `lib/engine.ts`, store chosen there (task 298). Plan 49 task 294: `engine/store.ts` `MemoryStore`, `lib/store.ts` `ServerStore`.
- Plan 51 (PORT-8) task 301: `/media` as cache-only lookup, `404 media_missing`. The shell copies that contract; it needn''t wait for it.
- Task 1 can land now (start screen only); tasks 2–3 wait for task 297/294; task 5 waits for task 298. A task whose dependency isn''t done stops and says so.

## Decisions taken here
- **Files:** `app/desktop/` (D-35): `package.json` (`"main": "main.mjs"`, `"type": "module"`, no dependencies), `main.mjs` (window, protocol, F11, security), `preload.cjs` (sandboxed preloads must be CommonJS), `resolve.mjs` (URL → file, pure). Plain JS, no build step, no npm workspace yet; part 3 makes it one when it adds `electron` + `electron-builder` (pin the npm `electron` to the major of the flake''s, today 43).
- **One origin, same URLs:** `protocol.handle("app")`, registered privileged (`standard`, `secure`, `supportFetchAPI`, `stream`); the window loads `app://trivia/`. Absolute paths in the client (`/assets/…`, `/fonts/…`, `/audio/…`, `/data/…`, `/media?url=…`) work unchanged; no adapter in `lib/` for URLs.
- **`resolve.mjs`** exports `makeResolver({dist, data, media}) → (Request) → Promise<Response>`, web `Request`/`Response` only (Node 22 has both), so a throw-away script tests it under plain `node`:
  - `/data/<path>` → file under `data` (resolve + containment check, like `send_static`), else `404 {"error":"not_found"}`.
  - `/media?url=<file_url>` → only URLs in `data/pool.json` (`picked`: `media.file_url`, `background.file_url`; the set is computed once at start) → `<media>/<sha1(url)[:16]><ext>`, the same rule as `app/server/media_cache.py` `cache_path` (lowercase ext matching `\.[a-z0-9]{1,5}`, else `.bin`; `node:crypto`). Missing → `404 {"error":"media_missing"}`; not in the pool → `404 {"error":"not_found"}`. No download, no network.
  - `Range` requests → `206` with `Content-Range` (video/audio seeking; don''t rely on `net.fetch(file:)` for ranges).
  - `/api/…` → `404 {"error":"not_found"}` (no Python API in the shell; the save goes through the bridge).
  - Anything else → file under `dist`, else `dist/index.html` (single-page app).
  - Explicit MIME map (html, js, css, json, woff2, m4a, mp3, ogg, oga, opus, wav, webm, mp4, jpg, jpeg, png, gif, webp, svg, avif); unknown → `application/octet-stream`.
- **Roots:** `main.mjs` `roots()`: dev = `app/client/dist`, `app/data`, `TRIVIA_MEDIA` or `<repo>/media`; `app.isPackaged` → under `process.resourcesPath` (exact layout is part 3''s). Missing `dist/index.html` → a dialog «client not built: run `npm run build -w app/client`» and quit.
- **Window:** `BrowserWindow` `fullscreen: true`, `show: false` until `ready-to-show`, background colour of the theme, no application menu (`Menu.setApplicationMenu(null)`). F11 in `webContents.on("before-input-event")` toggles `setFullScreen`; the key never reaches the page. Single-instance lock. `autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required` switch, so the first sound plays like after a click in the browser.
- **Security and offline:** `contextIsolation: true`, `sandbox: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`; `will-navigate` blocked unless `app://trivia/`; `setWindowOpenHandler` → deny; every `http(s)://` and `ws(s)://` request cancelled (`session.webRequest`); permission requests denied except `fullscreen`. DevTools only with `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`. No telemetry, no crash reporter upload.
- **Bridge (`preload.cjs`, `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld("trivia", …)`)**: `{desktop: true, toggleFullscreen(), quit()}` over `ipcRenderer.invoke` with fixed channel names; main checks the sender''s origin. SW-3 adds `loadSave`/`writeSave`, S5 the Steam calls. Typed in the client as `lib/desktop.ts`: `export const desktop: DesktopBridge | null` (`window.trivia ?? null`).
- **Client changes (only when `desktop` is set, browser setup unchanged, D-59):**
  - Overlay fullscreen button → `desktop.toggleFullscreen()`; DOM fullscreen otherwise.
  - Authoring links hidden (no authoring server; same as `VITE_AUTHORING_URL=""`).
  - «Salir del juego» in the ☰ overlay → `desktop.quit()` (the Deck has no window close). Through `t()` if LUI-1 (plan 21) has landed, else a Spanish literal marked like its neighbours.
  - Store: where plan 50''s `lib/engine.ts` creates `ServerStore`, `desktop ? new MemoryStore() : new ServerStore()`. The save is lost on quit until SW-3; acceptable for the skeleton.
- **NixOS dev:** `pkgs.electron` in the dev shell; `trivia-desktop` in `flake.nix` = `fromCheckout`-style `writeShellApplication` running `electron "$root/app/desktop" "$@"` (the npm Electron binary doesn''t run on NixOS). No `.#app` change (part 3 owns packaged builds). Headless checks: `xvfb-run` from nixpkgs (`nix shell nixpkgs#xvfb-run`) if no display.
- **Steam binding pick (SW-2''s second half):** a pm decision between steamworks-ffi-node and steamworks.js (maintenance, overlay on Windows/Linux/Deck, Electron 43 support, native module vs FFI and what electron-builder needs, licence). No dependency added in S3; SW-8 (task 255) builds on the answer.
- **Decision entry** (next D number in `plans/decisions.md`): the `app://` protocol and same-URL resolver; no network in the shell; bridge surface; `MemoryStore` until SW-3; dev Electron from nixpkgs.

## Files
- New: `app/desktop/package.json`, `main.mjs`, `preload.cjs`, `resolve.mjs`; `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts`.
- Change: `flake.nix` (dev shell `pkgs.electron`, `trivia-desktop`), `app/client/src/game/Overlay.svelte`, `app/client/src/lib/engine.ts` (store choice; plan 50''s file), `app/client/src/vite-env.d.ts` or `desktop.ts` (`Window.trivia` type).
- Docs: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-2 `[x]`), `plans/decisions.md`, `directory.md` (`app/desktop/`), `plans/19-repo-layout.md` (`app/desktop/` in the tree), AGENTS.md "Commands" (`trivia-desktop`), README.md (one line), `plans/project.md`.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Window, protocol skeleton, `trivia-desktop`** (can run now): `app/desktop/` with `main.mjs`, `package.json`, `resolve.mjs` serving `dist` only (SPA fallback, MIME map, `/api/…` 404); fullscreen, F11, single instance, security/offline rules; `flake.nix` dev shell + `trivia-desktop`. Check: `npm run build -w app/client`; `trivia-desktop` (or under `xvfb-run`) opens fullscreen and the start screen renders with both fonts; a throw-away script with `--remote-debugging-port` and Node''s built-in `WebSocket` (CDP `Runtime.evaluate`) reads `document.fonts` status, fetches `/audio/fanfarria.m4a` (200, `audio/mp4`), confirms `fetch("https://example.org")` fails, and `window.require` is undefined; F11 toggles (CDP `Input.dispatchKeyEvent` or `win.isFullScreen()` logged). Without `dist/` the dialog appears. The browser game (`trivia`) is unchanged. `nix flake check` or `nix develop -c true` evaluates.
2. **Data and media resolver** (needs task 297''s `/data/` URLs): `/data/…`, `/media?url=…` (pool set, `cache_path` rule, `media_missing`), `Range` → 206. Throw-away `node` script against `makeResolver` with a temp media dir: `cache_path` parity with Python for every URL in `app/data/pool.json` (run `media_cache.cache_path` in `python3` and compare); a cached file 200 with the right MIME and bytes; `Range: bytes=0-99` → 206, 100 bytes, correct `Content-Range`; uncached pool URL → `404 media_missing`; non-pool URL, `/data/../client/dist/index.html`, `/data/%2e%2e/…` → 404; `/data/pool.json` and every categories file plays back byte-equal. In the window: a video question seeks (CDP: set `currentTime`, `seeked` fires).
3. **Bridge and client adapter** (needs plan 49 task 294; the store line needs task 298, otherwise leave a `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)`-free TODO for task 5 and say so in the note): `preload.cjs`, IPC handlers with origin check, `lib/desktop.ts`, overlay fullscreen / «Salir del juego» / authoring links, store choice. Check: in `trivia-desktop` (CDP) `window.trivia.desktop === true`, `toggleFullscreen()` flips `isFullScreen`, `quit()` exits with code 0; in the browser (`trivia`, temp `TRIVIA_STATE`) the overlay looks and behaves as before (no «Salir», authoring links present, DOM fullscreen). `npm run check`, `npm run build`.
4. **Steam binding: facts and decision** (no code; can run any time): steamworks-ffi-node vs steamworks.js with sources and dates: last release, open issues, Electron 43 support, overlay status on Windows/Linux/Deck, how it loads (`koffi` FFI vs N-API prebuilds) and what that means for electron-builder (`asarUnpack`, `steam_api64.dll`/`libsteam_api.so` placement), licence. `pm decision add "Steam binding for the Electron shell?"` with the recommended option first, body ultra-short. Then a follow-up task in this plan, pending on it: record the answer in D-63 (consequences line) and plan 18 (SW-2 note, SW-8 wording).
5. **Whole game without Python, docs** (needs tasks 1–3 and 298; last): `pgrep -f app/server/main.py` empty, then `trivia-desktop` on a temp `TRIVIA_MEDIA` holding a synced copy of the approved media (or `TRIVIA_MEDIA=$PWD/media` read-only, asserted unchanged). Throw-away CDP script: start screen → new player → a whole game to level 12 or a loss, every joker once, admin overlay undo/abandon; per question with media the element reports loaded (`naturalWidth > 0`, `readyState ≥ 2`), no `mediaFailed`; the sound module''s samples decoded (no `fetch` error in the console); console free of errors; `pgrep` still empty at the end. Then a decision for the gamemaster "Desktop shell plays?": run `trivia-desktop`, play a short game with sound, F11, «Salir»; options "plays fine" (recommended), "problems (listed)". Docs in "Files" and the decision entry; SW-2 `[x]` in plan 18 with date and files (once the binding answer is recorded, else note it pending).

## Done when
- `trivia-desktop` opens the game fullscreen (F11 toggles) and a whole game plays with media and sound while no Python process runs.
- The page has no Node, no network; the bridge exposes only `desktop`, `toggleFullscreen`, `quit`.
- `/data/` and `/media?url=…` answer as the Python server does (same URLs, same cache file names, `media_missing`), with range requests.
- The browser game (`trivia`) is unchanged; `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass; no new npm dependencies.
- Steam binding decision asked (answer recorded or its follow-up task queued); decision entry, plan 18, `directory.md`, `19-repo-layout.md`, AGENTS.md, README.md match the code.', '2026-10-12T03:37:23Z', 209);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (55, 8, 'File saves (SW-3)', 470, 'The desktop shell (plan 54) keeps the save in memory; this plan writes it to one JSON file in the user''s config folder, so players and burned questions survive a restart and a crash. A `FileStore` in the client implements plan 49''s `Store` over the preload bridge; Electron''s main process does the file work (atomic write, Windows lock retry, backups). A corrupt or newer-version file is moved to a backup and the game starts fresh with a message. Part 2 of masterplan 8 (S3); owner `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-3). Builds: part 3 (task 211); Steam Auto-Cloud setup: S5 (plan 11 parts, tasks reading this plan''s path).

## Depends on
- Plan 54 (SW-2): `app/desktop/` (`main.mjs`, `preload.cjs`, origin-checked IPC), `lib/desktop.ts`, store choice in `lib/engine.ts` (`desktop ? MemoryStore : ServerStore`). Tasks 1–2 need its bridge task (plan 54 task 3); task 3 needs its whole-game task (plan 54 task 5).
- Plan 49 (PORT-4): `Store`, `SaveData`, `emptySave()`, `engine/save.ts` `parseSave`, `lib/store.ts` `ServerStore` (serialized, coalesced writes).
- Plan 21 (LUI-1): `t()` and the `es` catalog for the messages; plan 22''s `errorText` for `save_locked`. If plan 21 hasn''t landed, Spanish literals marked like their neighbours and a backlog line.
- A task whose dependency isn''t done stops and says so.

## Decisions taken here
- **Location** (fixed now; S5''s Auto-Cloud config and the gamemaster''s docs point at it):
  - Packaged: `app.setPath("userData", <appData>/trivia)` before `ready` (`%APPDATA%\trivia` on Windows, `~/.config/trivia` on Linux and the Deck), independent of the product name the builder sets later. Save: `<userData>/save/game.json`.
  - Dev (`!app.isPackaged`): `<repo>/state/desktop/game.json` (gitignored; never the browser game''s `state/game.json`).
  - `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` overrides both (every check uses a temp dir).
  - Temp file `save/game.json.tmp` (same dir, so rename is atomic); backups in `save/backup/`. Auto-Cloud (S5) syncs `save/` non-recursively with pattern `game.json`: temp and backups never sync.
- **Main is a dumb file store, like the Python server (plan 49):** validation stays in one place, `parseSave` in the client.
  - `app/desktop/save.mjs` (pure `node:fs`, no Electron import, testable under plain `node`): `makeSaveFile(dir, {rename = fs.rename})` → `{read(), write(text), backup(kind), dropStaleTemp()}`.
  - `read()` → text or `null` when missing.
  - `write(text)`: envelope check only (≤ 10 MB, parses to an object with numeric `version`), else `bad_save`; open `.tmp`, write, `fd.sync()`, close, `rename` over `game.json`. `EPERM`/`EBUSY`/`EACCES` → retry 10× / 100 ms, then `save_locked`; the old file stays intact, the `.tmp` is removed.
  - `backup(kind)` (`corrupt` | `newer`): rename `game.json` → `backup/game-<kind>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>.json` (suffix `-2`, `-3` on collision); returns the path. Never deletes a backup.
  - `dropStaleTemp()` at start: a leftover `.tmp` (crash mid-write) is deleted; `game.json` is the truth.
  - One writer: main queues writes (one in flight); `before-quit` waits for the in-flight write (`preventDefault`, then `app.quit()` again).
- **Bridge** (plan 54''s `window.trivia`, same origin check): `loadSave(): Promise<string|null>`, `writeSave(text): Promise<void>` (rejects with code `save_locked` | `bad_save`), `backupSave(kind): Promise<string>`. Typed in `lib/desktop.ts`.
- **`FileStore`** in `lib/store.ts`, next to `ServerStore`, sharing its serialize/coalesce queue (extract a small helper if `ServerStore` has it inline):
  - `load()`: `null` → `emptySave()`; else `parseSave(JSON.parse(text))`. On failure: kind `newer` when `version` > `SAVE_VERSION`, else `corrupt` (bad JSON, bad shape); `backupSave(kind)` first, then `emptySave()`, and `notice = {kind, path}`. Nothing is written before the backup succeeds; a failed backup throws (the game shows the error and doesn''t overwrite the file).
  - `parseSave` must tell "newer" apart: if plan 49''s error isn''t typed, add a code (`save_newer`) there.
  - `save()`: like `ServerStore`; a rejected write throws `GameError("save_locked")`, the in-memory save stays and the next action writes the whole document again (plan 50''s rule).
    - `save_locked` doesn''t fail the action (task 321): `lib/engine.ts` adopts the reply anyway and keeps the error (`saveError()`); the screens show it in the error corner until a write succeeds. Else the UI stays a step behind the in-memory save and the engine refuses the retry.
  - `flush()`: resolves when the queue is empty; «Salir del juego» awaits it before `desktop.quit()`.
- **Messages** (catalog keys, `es` first): `save.corrupt` «No se pudo leer la partida guardada. Se guardó una copia en {path} y empieza una partida nueva.», `save.newer` «La partida guardada es de una versión más nueva del juego. …» (same tail), `error.save_locked` «No se pudo guardar. Se intenta de nuevo con la próxima jugada.». Shown once on the start screen (dismissed with `confirm`, plan 44''s action layer if landed, else Enter/click).
- **Import of the browser save (cheap, so in):** `trivia-desktop --import-save <file>` (also works on the packaged binary): if no `game.json` exists, copy the file in with `write()`''s atomic path (envelope check); if one exists, refuse with a message on stderr and start normally. `parseSave` validates on load as usual. README: one line, plus "or copy `state/game.json` to the save folder".
- **Decision entry** (next D number): file location per OS + `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`, main as dumb store / client validates, temp + backup outside the synced pattern, corrupt/newer → backup + fresh + message, import flag.

## Files
- New: `app/desktop/save.mjs`.
- Change: `app/desktop/main.mjs` (userData path, IPC handlers, quit wait, `--import-save`), `app/desktop/preload.cjs`, `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts`, `lib/store.ts` (`FileStore`), `lib/engine.ts` (store choice, notice), `engine/save.ts` (typed newer error if needed), start screen (notice), Overlay «Salir» (flush), `es` catalog.
- Docs: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-3 `[x]`; Steam Cloud bullet: path and pattern), `plans/decisions.md`, `directory.md` (`app/desktop/save.mjs`, `state/desktop/`), README.md (save location, import), `plans/project.md`.

## Tasks to split into
1. **`save.mjs` + main wiring** (needs plan 54 task 3): `save.mjs`, userData path, IPC `save:load`/`save:write`/`save:backup`, write queue, quit wait, `dropStaleTemp`, `--import-save`; decision entry. Throw-away `node` script on a temp dir: read missing → `null`; write/read round trip byte-equal; injected `rename` failing `EPERM` 3× → ok, always → `save_locked` with old file byte-identical and no `.tmp`; > 10 MB, `[]`, `"x"`, no `version` → `bad_save`; two backups in the same second get distinct names; stale `.tmp` dropped, `game.json` untouched. Import: into an empty dir copies; with an existing save refuses and leaves it identical.
2. **Bridge, `FileStore`, messages** (needs task 1, plan 49 task 294, plan 50''s `lib/engine.ts`): preload methods, `lib/desktop.ts` types, `FileStore`, store choice, notice on the start screen, catalog keys, flush before «Salir». Check with a throw-away CDP script (plan 54''s pattern) under `trivia-desktop`, `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` temp: create a player, answer one question, «Salir» → exit 0; restart → player and burned question there, the game resumes. Garbage `game.json` → backup file with the original bytes, fresh save, `save.corrupt` text on screen; `version: 2` → `save.newer`; read-only `save/` dir (Linux stand-in for a lock) → `save_locked` text, game continues, next action after `chmod u+w` writes. Browser game (`trivia`, temp `TRIVIA_STATE`) unchanged. `npm run check`, `npm run build`.
3. **Crash test, docs** (needs task 2 and plan 54 task 5): throw-away script: `trivia-desktop` on a temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`; via CDP drive actions in a loop (or call `store.save` with a padded multi-MB document so writes take time) and `SIGKILL` the Electron main process at random times, ≥ 50 rounds; after each kill `game.json` parses with `parseSave` and equals one of the documents sent, and the next start removes any `.tmp` and loads it. Then the docs in "Files"; SW-3 `[x]` in plan 18 with date and files.

## Done when
- In `trivia-desktop`, players and burned questions survive a restart, and the kill loop never leaves an unreadable or partial `game.json`.
- Corrupt and newer-version files end up in `save/backup/` byte-identical, the game starts fresh and says so in Spanish through the catalog.
- A simulated lock shows `save_locked` without losing the in-memory game; `--import-save` brings a browser save over.
- The browser game is unchanged; `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass; no new dependencies.
- Plan 18, the decision entry, `directory.md` and README match the code.', '2026-10-12T03:44:11Z', 210);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (56, 8, 'Local builds for Windows and Linux (SW-5, SW-6)', 460, 'electron-builder turns the desktop shell (plan 54) with file saves (plan 55) into two artefacts a family can unpack and play offline: a Windows x64 zip and a Linux x64 tar.gz (the Deck runs the Linux one). One command builds both on the gamemaster''s Linux machine: export check, client build, media staged from the approved cache (~720 MB, as is; resizing is SW-9, S5), packaging. The start test on a clean Windows machine and a Linux machine without Nix is a written checklist the gamemaster runs. Part 3 of masterplan 8 (S3); owner `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Builds and depots", SW-5, SW-6).

## Depends on
- Plan 54 (SW-2): `app/desktop/` (`main.mjs` `roots()` with an `app.isPackaged` branch, `resolve.mjs` with the `cache_path` rule), `trivia-desktop`. Tasks 1–2 need its tasks 1–3 (314–316); task 2''s full game needs its task 5 (318).
- Plan 55 (SW-3): save in `<appData>/trivia/save/game.json` when packaged, `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`. Task 2''s restart check needs its task 2 (321).
- Plan 47 (PUB-5): `dist/CREDITS.md`, `app/client/credits.ts`. Conditional: copied / extended only if present; no wait.
- Plan 45 / 46: nothing; their pad and Deck checks run on these artefacts in plan 48.
- pm decision 14 "CI builds (SW-6): in S3 or S5, and with or without media?": task 5 waits for it. Tasks 1–4 don''t.
- A task whose dependency isn''t done stops and says so.

## Decisions taken here
- **Targets:** Windows x64 `zip` (portable, no installer: Steam installs folders, an installer is dead weight), Linux x64 `tar.gz` (no AppImage: needs FUSE, Steam/Deck run a folder; its tooling doesn''t run on NixOS). Both built on Linux; no wine: `win.signAndEditExecutable: false`, so the exe keeps Electron''s icon and file metadata (backlog: icon + metadata in S5, with SW-6 or a Windows machine). Unsigned: SmartScreen warns on a downloaded zip; checklist row.
- **Names:** `productName` "Trivia", `appId` `io.github.rubenmoor.trivia`, executable `trivia` / `Trivia.exe`, version from `app/desktop/package.json` (= flake''s `version`). Artefacts `Trivia-<version>-win-x64.zip`, `Trivia-<version>-linux-x64.tar.gz` in `app/desktop/release/` (gitignored).
- **Packaging (no npm workspace):** `app/desktop/` gets its own `package-lock.json` with devDependencies `electron` (exact 43.x, the flake''s major) and `electron-builder`; not in the root `workspaces`. Why: `npm install` for the game and `nix build .#app` (its `npmDepsHash`) stay untouched (D-59), and Electron''s binary download never enters the game''s install. Overrides plan 54''s "part 3 makes it a workspace"; note it in the decision entry. Config in `app/desktop/electron-builder.yml`.
- **Layout in the artefact:** `resources/app.asar` = `package.json`, `*.mjs`, `preload.cjs` only (`files` whitelist; no `node_modules`, no build dir). `extraResources`: `../client/dist` → `resources/client`, `../data` → `resources/data`, `build/media` → `resources/media`. Media outside the asar so S5 can ship it as the shared content depot (plan 18) without repacking. `CREDITS.md` from `dist/` also at the artefact root (`extraFiles`), next to Electron''s `LICENSE.electron.txt` and `LICENSES.chromium.html`.
- **`roots()` packaged branch** (plan 54 left the layout to this plan): `client`, `data`, `media` under `process.resourcesPath`; `TRIVIA_MEDIA` still overrides media (a no-media build can point at a folder).
- **Media staging:** `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs` (plain `node`, no Electron): reads `app/data/pool.json`, every `file_url` of `media` and `background` (the resolver''s set), maps each through the shared `cache_path` function (exported from `resolve.mjs`, not copied), hard-links (fallback copy) from `TRIVIA_MEDIA` or `<repo>/media` into `app/desktop/build/media/` after emptying it. Missing files → exit 1 listing them and «run `trivia-media sync --status approved`»; `--allow-missing` builds anyway (the game shows its missing-media notice). Prints count and MB. Only pool files ship, never the rest of the 3 GB cache.
- **Build command:** `npm run dist --prefix app/desktop` = `npm run build -w app/client` (from the root), `stage-media`, `electron-builder --x64 --linux tar.gz --win zip`. The flake adds `trivia-desktop-build` (`fromCheckout`-style): `qgen validate` (fails on a stale `app/data/pool.json`) first, then the npm script with `ELECTRON_SKIP_BINARY_DOWNLOAD=1` (the npm Electron binary is useless on NixOS; electron-builder fetches the Windows/Linux zips into `~/.cache/electron` once, later builds run offline). If electron-builder''s helper binaries don''t run on NixOS, run them through `steam-run` in the wrapper and say so in the decision entry. `qgen validate` lives in the wrapper, not the npm script: `app/` never calls `authoring/`.
- **Linux sandbox:** a `tar.gz` has no SUID `chrome-sandbox`, and Ubuntu ≥ 24.04 and Steam''s runtime block unprivileged user namespaces, so Electron fails to start. The Linux executable gets `--no-sandbox` through electron-builder''s `linux.executableArgs` (if that only applies to desktop files: an `afterPack` hook that renames the binary to `trivia-bin` and writes a `trivia` shell launcher). Same as electron-builder''s AppImage default; the page is local, has no Node and no network (plan 54). Windows keeps the sandbox.
- **Offline:** no auto-updater, no crash upload, no network at runtime (plan 54''s rules hold in the package; task 2 checks with no network namespace).
- **Decision entry** (next D number): targets and why, own lockfile instead of workspace, artefact layout (media outside the asar), staging rule, `--no-sandbox` on Linux, unsigned exe until S5.

## Files
- New: `app/desktop/electron-builder.yml`, `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs`, `app/desktop/package-lock.json`, possibly `app/desktop/after-pack.mjs` (Linux launcher).
- Change: `app/desktop/package.json` (devDependencies, scripts `dist`, `stage-media`), `app/desktop/main.mjs` (`roots()` packaged branch), `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` (export `cachePath`), `.gitignore` (`app/desktop/build/`, `app/desktop/release/`), `flake.nix` (`trivia-desktop-build` in the dev shell; `.#app` unchanged).
- If `app/client/credits.ts` exists (plan 47): Electron entry under Libraries (MIT, pointing at `LICENSE.electron.txt` and `LICENSES.chromium.html` shipped beside it).
- Docs: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-5 `[x]`, "Builds and depots" rewritten for S3: local command, layout, targets; new section "Local build start test"), `plans/decisions.md`, `directory.md` (`app/desktop/` new files, `build/`, `release/`), `plans/19-repo-layout.md`, AGENTS.md "Commands" (`trivia-desktop-build`), README.md (build and run the desktop game; where to put `CREDITS.md`/media is automatic), `plans/project.md`.

## Tasks to split into
1. **electron-builder config, packaged layout, `trivia-desktop-build`** (needs plan 54 tasks 314–316): own lockfile, `electron-builder.yml`, `roots()` packaged branch, Linux `--no-sandbox`, `stage-media.mjs`, npm script, flake command, `.gitignore`. Check: `trivia-desktop-build` produces both artefacts from a clean `app/desktop/build` + `release`; a throw-away script lists the zip and tar.gz (`Trivia.exe` / `trivia`, `resources/app.asar` holding only the whitelist, `resources/client/index.html`, `resources/data/pool.json` byte-equal to `app/data/pool.json`, `resources/media` file count = distinct pool URLs, `CREDITS.md` at the root if plan 47 landed); staging with one cache file renamed away → exit 1 naming it, `--allow-missing` → builds; a second build with the network off (`unshare -rn`) succeeds from the cache. `npm install` at the root and `nix build .#app` unchanged (`git diff package-lock.json` empty, `.#app` builds). Decision entry.
2. **Packaged Linux build plays offline, docs** (needs task 1, plan 54 task 318, plan 55 task 321): unpack the tar.gz into a temp dir, run it outside the Nix shell environment (`steam-run`, or `env -i` with only `HOME`, `DISPLAY`/`xvfb-run`) under `unshare -rn` (no network) with a temp `HOME` / `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` unset (so the packaged save path is used under the temp `HOME`). Plan 54''s throw-away CDP script (start the binary with `--remote-debugging-port`, accepted only with `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`, as in plan 54): new player → a short game with an image, audio and video question (media loaded, no `mediaFailed`), quit, restart → player and burned questions there; `<HOME>/.config/trivia/save/game.json` exists; `pgrep -f app/server/main.py` empty; no file outside the temp dirs written. Windows: content listing only (no wine); the start test is the gamemaster''s. Docs in "Files"; SW-5 stays `[ ]` until task 4.
3. **Local build start test: checklist and decision** (after task 2): section "Local build start test" in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (after "Builds and depots"): how to get the artefacts (command, or the zip/tar.gz the gamemaster copies over), one table per machine — Windows x64 without Node/Python, Linux x64 without Nix (e.g. Ubuntu 24.04) — columns check | result | note; rows: network off before unpacking; unpack and start (SmartScreen «More info → Run anyway» expected on Windows; `./trivia` on Linux); fullscreen, F11 toggles; keyboard game to level 3 with an image, audio and video question and sound; quit and restart keeps the player; save file at `%APPDATA%\trivia\save\game.json` / `~/.config/trivia/save/game.json`; `CREDITS.md` in the folder; no console window (Windows). Plan 48 merges this section into its S3 platform test (link it there in its task note, not by editing plan 48). Then `did=$(pm decision add "Local builds start offline?" …)` with the checklist in the body and the build commit; options "both pass", "issues (fill the tables)"; `pm task-pending-decision` task 4 on it.
4. **Record the start test** (waits for task 3''s decision): fill the tables (date, build commit). Pass → SW-5 `[x]` in plan 18 with date and files, `plans/project.md`. Issues → per failing row a task in this plan (or plan 54/55 if it''s theirs) with the row and how to reproduce, then a re-test decision with the failed rows and this task pending on it; stage and stop without closing.
5. **CI (SW-6) per decision 14** (waits for decision 14): "Move to S5" → SW-6 note in plan 18 («moved to S5, decision 14»), `plans/11-steam.md` S3 row SW-1..SW-5 and S5 row gains SW-6, decision entry line, `plans/project.md`; no code. "Keep, without media" → `.github/workflows/desktop.yml`: `ubuntu-latest`, Node 22, `npm ci`, `npm ci --prefix app/desktop`, `npm run dist --prefix app/desktop` with `stage-media --allow-missing` (no Python, no `qgen validate`: CI trusts the committed `pool.json`; `qgen validate` stays the local gate), artefacts uploaded as workflow artefacts, no secrets; on push to `main` and manual. Check with `act` if in nixpkgs, else push and read the run (`gh run watch`). "Keep, with media" → as before plus Python + `trivia-media sync --status approved` with `actions/cache` keyed on the hash of `pool.json`''s URL list; one run must pass. Then SW-6 `[x]` and docs.

## Done when
- `trivia-desktop-build` (or `npm run dist --prefix app/desktop` outside Nix) produces `Trivia-<version>-win-x64.zip` and `Trivia-<version>-linux-x64.tar.gz` with client, data, staged media and `CREDITS.md` (if plan 47 landed).
- The unpacked Linux build plays a game with media and sound, no network and no Python, and keeps the save across a restart; the gamemaster''s start test (decision from task 3) passes on Windows and non-Nix Linux.
- `npm install`, `npm run build`, `nix build .#app` and the `trivia` game are unchanged (D-59); no new dependencies beyond `electron` and `electron-builder` (dev, in `app/desktop/`).
- SW-6 resolved per decision 14; plan 18, the decision entry, `directory.md`, `19-repo-layout.md`, AGENTS.md, README.md match the code.', '2026-10-12T03:47:41Z', 211);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (57, 9, 'Release quality bar and back-audit (CT-5)', 640, 'Part 2 of the masterplan (plan 9), owner `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Quality bar", CT-5). D-56 (plan 16, pm decision 2: 30 spot-checked per batch, ≥ 90 % agreement in the last two batches) covers batches from batch-8 on. The 1136 questions approved before it (pilot 73, first-120 116, batch-3 112, batch-4 108, batch-5 83, batch-6 76, batch-7 568; incl. `colombia`) never had an audit or a spot check, except batch-7''s audit sample (60, task 46). This plan sets the bar a batch must meet for the Steam release, what happens to a batch above the error limit, and audits the old pool in slices so it meets the same bar. Tooling and procedure only; the gamemaster starts every slice.

## Preconditions
- Plan 16 done (tasks 46, 47, 48, 49): `qgen audit`, `audit_sample`, `spot-checks.json`, `/review?…&sample=1`, `audit=flagged`, `qgen report --qc`, `authoring/QC.md`. Task 48 (`--qc`, trend, `quality` keys) must be done before task 1 here.
- pm decision 15 (release bar: D-56''s numbers or stricter): blocks tasks 1 and 4. Recommended: D-56''s agreement plus ≤ 2 false approves in the 30 and none of kind `fact`.

## Release bar
- New keys `quality.release` in `authoring/data/targets.json` (D-53''s file): `max_false_approve`, `max_fact_false_approve`, `spot_check_size` (values from decision 15; option 2 → only `min_agreement` reused). `qgen validate` checks them.
- Applies per batch and per back-audit slice, per language later (translations: native speaker, plan 9 rules).
- `qgen report --qc` (trend) gets a row "release" ✓/✗ per batch/slice; `qgen report --qc <batch>` states which limit failed.
- Above the limit → the batch or slice is **not release-ready** (family play unchanged; statuses stay as the gamemaster decided):
  1. `qgen audit --batch <b> --all`: audit every approved question of it, not only the sample (skips audited ones).
  2. Gamemaster decides the flagged ones in `/review?batch=<b>&audit=flagged`.
  3. Second spot check with a new seed (`<b>#2`), excluding already spot-checked ids; release-ready once it passes.
- Release-ready state per batch/slice in `authoring/data/spot-checks.json` (derived from its items, not stored twice) and listed by `qgen report --qc`. Part 12 (S4 close-out) reads it: every batch/slice with approved questions in the release pool is release-ready.
- D-entry (D-65 or next free): release bar, consequence, back-audit. QC.md gets a "Release bar" step after step 3.

## Back-audit
- `qgen audit --backlog [--slice N]` (N default 200): gamemaster asks, like `qgen rework`; never part of `qgen batch`, so RUNBOOK/D-36 unchanged except one line under "only when the gamemaster asks".
  - Creates `work/backaudit-<k>/run.json` (`mode: backaudit`, `ids`, `started`) with the next N approved questions without any audit, oldest batch first (pilot → batch-7); resumes an unfinished run first (like `cmd_rework`).
  - One opus call per question, `prompts/audit.md` unchanged, `work/backaudit-<k>/audit/<id>.json`; `costs.log` there. Never changes the pool.
- `spot_checks.audit_of(q)`: also finds audits in `backaudit-*` runs (newest wins); small index, not a glob per question.
- Findings → review tool: `/review?run=backaudit-<k>&audit=flagged` (major findings, audit notes beside the review''s), and `&sample=1` for the slice''s blind spot check (30 random approved ids of the slice, seeded by run name; `spot_checks.record` accepts run membership, not only `q.batch`).
- Report: `authoring/reports/backaudit-<k>.md` with the Audit section (`audit_section` reused) and the QC section after the spot check.
- Per slice, as for a batch (QC.md): back-audit → spot-check decision (gamemaster) → `qgen report --qc backaudit-<k>` → release bar → QC proposals decision if findings. Flagged questions the gamemaster sends to needs_work go through `qgen rework` later (gamemaster asks).

## Cost
- Baseline: batch-7 audit, 60 opus calls, $2.75 (≈ $0.046 per question, `work/batch-7/audit/costs.log`).
- Estimate: ~1080 unaudited approved → ~$50, 6 slices of 200, ~1 h opus time with 3 jobs; spot checks 6 × 30 (~1.5 h of the gamemaster).
- Pilot slice first (100, the oldest: pilot + start of first-120); then a pm decision with the measured cost per question, flagged rate and the estimate for the rest ("Back-audit: run the remaining slices?", options all / only batch-7 / stop) before any further slice.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. Release bar keys and checks: `quality.release` in `targets.json` + `qgen validate`; release row in `qgen report --qc`, failed limit in the QC section; `qgen audit --batch <b> --all`; second spot-check seed (`<b>#2`, excluding checked ids) in `spot_checks.sample` and the review page; QC.md "Release bar" step; D-entry. Pending on decision 15. Done when: `qgen validate`, `npm run check` clean; `qgen report --qc` shows the release row for batch-7/batch-8 data present.
2. Back-audit command: `qgen audit --backlog [--slice N]`, `backaudit-<k>` runs, `audit_of` index, report file. Done when: a dry run with `--slice 3` on a scratch copy (or `--dry-run` listing ids) works, `qgen validate` clean; no real slice run.
3. Review tool for runs: `/review?run=<run>&audit=flagged` and `&sample=1` for back-audit runs; `spot_checks.record` by run membership; docstring lines in `main.py`. Done when: `npm run check` clean, checked in the browser with `trivia-authoring` on a 3-question test run (test entries removed).
4. Pilot slice (100) through the procedure: `qgen audit --backlog --slice 100`, spot-check decision, `--qc`, then the cost decision above. Priority -90 (with the content runs, after the batch tasks'' QC changes); runs only when the gamemaster has asked (task body says so).
5. Remaining slices: one task per slice, created by task 4''s worker after the cost decision is answered (option "all"/"only batch-7"); each ends at its spot-check and QC decisions like plan 17''s pattern. Priority -105 (after plan 17''s batch runs at -100, so batch QC changes land first).
6. Close CT-5 in `plans/16-content-target.md` (quality bar section: release bar, back-audit result per slice, cost), `plans/project.md`; after task 5.

## Done when
- The release bar is in `targets.json`, checked by `qgen report --qc`, and documented (QC.md, D-entry).
- Every approved question approved before D-56 has an audit, and every slice is release-ready or has a decision why not.
- `plans/16-content-target.md` CT-5 `[x]` with the numbers.', '2026-10-12T04:02:41Z', 241);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (58, 1, 'Fable as an opt-in model for qgen rework', 650, '`qgen rework` sends needs_work questions with specific feedback (giveaway, ambiguity, difficulty, overlap) once more through fix and review. These are the hardest cases and the volume is small, so a stronger model may pay off there first. This plan adds an opt-in `--model fable` to `qgen rework`, runs one experiment and lets the gamemaster decide from the numbers. Nothing changes for `qgen batch`. Sits next to plan 16 (quality control); its approval rate is a quality signal, not a replacement for QC.

## Today
- Every pipeline step is `claude()` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py` → `claude -p --model <x>`; `claude --help` lists `fable` as an alias next to `opus`, `sonnet`.
- Models hard-coded in `cmd_rework`: fix `opus` (fact check `check_model="sonnet"`), review 1 + 2 `REVIEW_MODEL = "opus"`.
- Model already recorded per call: `work/<run>/costs.log` (model, cost) and `review.model` on the question. No new bookkeeping needed.

## Cost facts (list prices)
- Fable 5.1 $10/$50 per MTok vs. Opus 5.5 $4/$20: 2.5× per token, more since Fable always thinks.
- rework-1: 43 questions, 54 calls, $5.57 (~$0.13/question) → Fable roughly $14+.
- batch-7: 964 calls, $120.74, mostly per-question review (~616 calls) → Fable for batch review ≈ +$150–200 per batch. Out of scope unless the experiment says otherwise.
- Subscription quota in dollars unpublished, also whether Fable shares Opus''s limit: gamemaster checks `/usage` before and after the run.

## The flag
- `qgen rework --model {opus,fable}`, default `opus`.
- Switches the fix step (`cmd_fix` `model`); fact check stays `sonnet`.
- Review 1 inside rework: also switched by default with the flag (it decides keep/fix after the reworked fix); review 2 stays `REVIEW_MODEL` (opus) so the final verdict is comparable to rework-1. Note this choice in the D-entry.
- Model stored in `run.json` (`"model"`), so a resumed run keeps it; `--model` on resume is ignored with a notice, like `--batch`.
- `qgen batch`, `qgen tighten`, `REVIEW_MODEL` unchanged.
- D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` when the flag lands. RUNBOOK unchanged unless the default changes. AGENTS.md command list: mention `--model fable` next to `qgen rework`.

## The experiment
- Only when the gamemaster asks for the next rework (AGENTS.md: `qgen rework` only on the gamemaster''s word): run it once with `--model fable`.
- Compare against rework-1 (43 questions, 54 calls, $5.57): approval rate after review 2, cost per question and per approved question (`costs.log`), needs_work reasons left, `/usage` delta.
- Result as a pm decision: keep Fable for rework (→ default change, RUNBOOK + D-entry update) / drop it / try Fable for batch review (→ new plan).

## Tasks (for the split)
1. Implement `qgen rework --model`, run.json persistence, D-entry, AGENTS.md line. Verify with a throw-away `--dry`-style check of the step namespaces (no paid run).
2. Experiment run + comparison note + decision. Blocked on the gamemaster asking for a rework (pending decision "run the next rework with Fable?"); priority -100 like batch runs (plan 17).

## Done when
- The flag exists, defaults to opus, D-entry written.
- One Fable rework run compared with rework-1, and the gamemaster has answered the keep/drop/extend decision.', '2026-10-12T04:11:20Z', 341);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (59, 7, 'Gamemaster mode: configure screen and gamemaster menu (MD-10..MD-12)', 480, 'Part 11 of the masterplan (plan 7). Gamemaster mode is today''s game, kept: one person, the gamemaster, holds every control, configures each game on a "configure game" screen and cheats freely through the gamemaster menu (`Esc`). Today''s overlay (undo, skip, skip and burn for everyone, joker budget MD-4, sound, restart) becomes that menu and grows. Owner: `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Gamemaster mode", tasks MD-10..MD-12.

## Depends on (tasks wait; no second implementation in `app/server/game.py`)
- Plan 35 (OQ-30, MD-5): rewrites plan 13 "Modes" to the five modes. This plan only owns the gamemaster-mode details (fields, cheats); it doesn''t re-record the modes.
- Plan 36 (MD-6, MD-7, 490): `settings.mode` (missing = `"gamemaster"`), the standard joker set constant, `settings.customized`, the mode screen and the refusals outside gamemaster mode. Reuse them; don''t add a second mode field.
- Plan 29 (Choice screen: age group + bundles, 400): the configure screen is plan 29''s Choice screen in its gamemaster-mode form, extended with the decided fields. No second screen with the same choices.
- Engine (plan 20, done) and screens on the engine (plan 50, PORT-7): `engine/game.ts`, `engine/api.ts`, `SaveData`, `lib/api.ts`.
- Action layer (IN-2..IN-5, done, pm plans 44/45): `lib/input.svelte.ts`, `lib/focus.ts`, `lib/gamepad.ts`; new controls declare scopes and `data-nav`, no `keydown`.
- Catalog (plan 21, done): every new string through `t()` (`configure.*`, `overlay.*`), `npm run check:literals` passes.
- Each implementation task first checks `pm show` for its dependencies; if one hasn''t landed, it leaves the task open and stops.

## Decisions taken here
- **Engine settings extend `settings`**, each new field optional with today''s behaviour as default (`withDefaults`), so old saves and the fixture replay are unchanged.
- **Cheats live in the engine** as actions in `engine/api.ts` (like `skip`, `undo`, `jokers`), refused (`409`, reason) when `settings.mode` isn''t `"gamemaster"`. Any cheat marks nothing for achievements: gamemaster mode has none (milestone 7).
- **Defaults** (D-88, pm decision 33): the configure screen opens on the player''s last game''s settings, so Enter straight through on an existing save plays as today; a fresh player gets the standard joker set, `young_teens`, the locale''s first base bundle. Games without the new fields and `new` without them play as before.

## Tasks
1. **Proposals and decisions: configure fields and cheat list**
   - Write two proposals into plan 13 "Gamemaster mode", from the code (`Overlay.svelte`, `engine/game.ts`, `engine/state.ts`, plan 29''s Choice screen):
     - Configure screen fields. Start from: age group, bundles (plan 29), joker set (unlimited / «Como las cartas» / standard set / custom per joker), media on/off; candidates to weigh: start level, extra fields that already exist as engine levers. Each with its default (= today) and its key.
     - Cheat list for the menu. Today: continue, skip, skip and burn for everyone, undo, joker budget, sound, fullscreen, restart, quit (desktop). New: manage jokers (give back / take away during the game), replace the current question (new draw at the same level and category; burn or not), candidates: jump to a level, reveal the answer to the gamemaster, change age group or bundles mid-game.
   - `pm decision add` twice: "Configure game screen: which fields?" and "Gamemaster menu: which cheats?"; option 1 = as proposed in plan 13 (recommended), option 2 = a shorter list named in the body; body = context + trade-offs, ultra-short.
   - `pm task-pending-decision` tasks 2–4 on the decision(s) they need (2: both; 3: fields; 4: cheats).
2. **Record the answers**: next free D-number in `plans/decisions.md` (D-73 is taken: local builds); plan 13 "Gamemaster mode": decided fields and cheats as a spec with the `settings` fields and engine actions; MD-10 `[x]` if the action layer already covers it (check: keyboard, mouse and pad each reach every control incl. the menu; else note what''s missing for task 4).
3. **Configure game screen (MD-11)**: engine settings fields + `newGame` accepts them; plan 29''s Choice screen in gamemaster mode shows the decided fields (focus, keys, pad); `lib/types.ts`. Check: `npm test` (fixture replay unchanged), `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `check:literals`; throw-away script: each field changes the new game as decided; browser walk: Enter straight through on an existing save = today''s game. Then MD-11 `[x]`.
4. **Gamemaster menu (MD-12)**: new engine actions per decided cheat (refused outside gamemaster mode); `Overlay.svelte` grows into the menu (today''s items kept, new ones added; keyboard, mouse and pad). Check: `npm test`, `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `check:literals`; throw-away script per cheat (state change, burn rows, undo after a cheat); browser walk with keyboard only, mouse only and pad. Then MD-12 `[x]`; docs: `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` (configure screen, menu, keys), `directory.md` if files were added, `plans/project.md` if MD-10..MD-12 are listed.

## Done when
- A gamemaster-mode game starts from the configure screen.
- The menu offers the decided cheats; each is refused outside gamemaster mode.
- The family''s game with defaults plays as today (fixture replay passes, Enter straight through).', '2026-10-12T16:44:17Z', 370);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (60, 12, 'masterplan', 1000, 'tbd.', '2026-10-12T16:46:08Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (61, 7, 'Competitive timed: record the revised spec (OQ-37 follow-up)', 580, 'Task 394 revised masterplan parts 5 and 8: competitive (timed) is now the milestone''s version and replaces decision 23''s timed part (own tracks, three levels behind, timeout ends the game). The recorded files still describe the old version. Plans 38 and 41 are done, so this plan brings the files in line. No new pm decisions: the milestone text ("Game modes", "Competitive (timed)") is the answer. Check stale spots with `grep -n -i timed plans/`.

## Spec to record (from milestone 7)
- 12 rounds; round = level (question difficulty follows the round); questions per round = number of players; one age group; no jokers.
- Every question shown to all players: 30 s, a hint every 8 s; unclaimed at 30 s = next question, nothing else.
- Claim: own action, any player, any time → that player has 6 s to answer; 6 s timeout = wrong answer; after the answer is shown, the next question comes; players may claim again after scoring.
- Lives: three each; round end: no correct answer in that round = −1 life; wrong answer (or claim timeout) = out at once; third life lost = out.
- Round 12 sudden death: first claim + correct answer wins at once; only one player left wins at once.
- Visuals: rounds and hearts; a heart pulses at a player''s last chance in a round without a correct answer (stronger on the last heart); last 3 s of a claim: clock ticks once per second, louder each tick, plus pulsing red frame; same red frame when everyone is at risk at once (all on last life, nobody correct this round).
- Open detail (not a decision): after drop-outs, do questions per round follow the players still in?

## Files
- `plans/decisions.md`: new D-entry (next free number; the file never edits old entries, a new entry supersedes) that supersedes D-77''s timed bullet and its timed burn multiplier; D-75''s burns-per-game line covered by the same entry ("Supersedes / related: D-77 (timed part), D-75 (timed burns), pm decision 23").
- `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Competitive timed": rewritten to the spec above; the open detail listed; MD-8 and MD-9 wording to match (claim action instead of per-player answer input), pointing to the new D-entry.
- `plans/14-input.md` section 3 and IN-6: the claim action (any player, any time, during `timed`) instead of "everyone answers at once"; per-player claim keys on the shared keyboard (claiming player then gets keyboard and mouse for the 6 s).
- `plans/16-content-target.md` burns per mode: timed ≈ N questions per round (N players) for up to 12 rounds, fewer after drop-outs, no jokers. Decision 21''s answer (D-75: no games number, 5000 per language) doesn''t depend on it: no new decision.
- `plans/open-questions.md` OQ-37 line and `plans/11-steam.md` OQ-37 row: add the new D-entry next to D-77.

## Done when
- `grep -n -i "three levels behind\|everyone answers\|answers at once\|1 shared question" plans/` finds nothing outside D-77 itself; the new D-entry exists and the files above point to it.', '2026-10-12T17:43:02Z', 402);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (62, 9, 'Simulation: games per new player (CT-2)', 570, 'CT-2 (`plans/16-content-target.md`, "Metric"): `qgen report --simulate` plays game after game for new players on the TS engine until the supply check fails. It reports games per new player per launch language, bundle set, mode and age group. The games numbers are **information only** (pm decision 21, D-75). Pass/fail is D-75''s target: 5000 approved per launch language with D-53''s per-level mix. That pass/fail is what milestone 9''s "Done when" and part 12 (S4 close-out) read. Part 9 (CT-3/CT-4, gap plan) reads the bottlenecks.

## Decisions this builds on
- D-74 (pm decision 19): no presets or checkpoint; modes `solo`, `rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`, `timed` (+ `gamemaster`); standard joker set `STANDARD_JOKERS` (3 × Soplo, 1 × each other joker) for every age group.
- D-75 (pm decision 21): target 5000 approved per launch language, D-53''s mix; no games-per-player bar.
- D-77, D-80 (pm decision 23): burns per mode. `rr-coop` = one game''s burns; `rr-competitive` ≈ N × one game; `timed` ≈ N questions per round, up to 12 rounds, no jokers.
- D-78 (pm decision 26): launch languages `es`, `en`, `de`.
- D-60: authoring runs the engine under plain Node 22 (type stripping), no Python copy. D-58: injected `Rng`. D-76: age-group windows and level weights.

## Where the code stands (2026-10-12)
- Engine done enough: `app/client/src/engine/game.ts` (`newGame`, `pick`, `answer`, `joker`, `supply`, `ChoiceArgs` with `age_group`, `bundles`, `mode`), `selection.ts`, `state.ts` (`engineData`, `emptySave`, `Io`), `rng.ts`; age groups and the bundle filter are in `resolveChoice` (plan 27). `BUILT_MODES` = `gamemaster`, `solo`.
- No Node entry point yet: `qgen report` still imports `app/server/selection.py`. PORT-8 (pm plan 51) moves the supply check to `node`. This plan writes the shared loader that plan 51 reuses (or reuses plan 51''s, whichever lands first).
- Per-locale pools (`app/data/pool.<locale>.json`) come from part 3 (task 242, not yet a plan). Until then only `es` = `app/data/pool.json` exists.

## Design
- **Node side** (`authoring/tools/sim/`, imports `app/client/src/engine/*.ts`, `.ts` extensions, erasable syntax only; `authoring/` may import `app/`, D-35):
  - `load.ts`: reads `app/data/` (pool for a locale, categories, bundles, age groups) → `EngineData`. The one loader for every Node entry point (plan 51''s supply call too).
  - `simulate.ts`: CLI, arguments as JSON on stdin, result as JSON on stdout. Python never re-implements a rule.
- **Referee = the engine.** One in-memory `SaveData` per run, `Io` with a seeded `Rng` and a fixed `now`. A game goes `newGame` → `pick` (random card of 4) → `joker` per policy → `answer`. The game count stops when `newGame` throws the supply error (`supply_short` or whatever `newGame` throws today). The bottleneck = the first `missing` level of that error, mapped to its difficulty range and the subcategories that ran dry at it.
- **Player models:**
  - `strong`: always right, reaches 12 every game. Burns the most per game, so it gives the lower bound.
  - `typical` (default): right with probability p(level), falling linearly from 0.95 at level 1 to 0.6 at level 12. A constant in `simulate.ts`, printed in the report header. Only a model; tune it later from real play if needed.
- **Joker policy** (standard set; `gamemaster` mode is not simulated): each joker is played once at a random level where the engine allows it. Soplo burns nothing; Saltar, Bájale and Cambiazo burn the swapped question; a Francotirador hit on the correct answer repeats the level with fresh cards. When the engine refuses a joker (supply), the joker is skipped, not forced.
- **Modes:**
  - `solo`, `rr-coop`: one engine game per game, same burns (D-77).
  - `rr-competitive` (`--players N`): N player names in one save; a "session" = one engine game per player, and every question shown burns for all N players (all of them see the screen). Until MD-8 is built, this is modelled by N `solo` games with the shown ids written as burns for all N players. Same draw and burn code from the engine, no rule copy.
  - `timed` (`--players N`): not in the engine yet (MD-9). Model: up to 12 rounds, N questions per round drawn with `selection.draw` at the round''s level ranges, burned for all N players. Drop-outs follow the `typical` p(level) per player; `strong` = nobody drops out. Replace it with the engine''s `timed` once MD-9 lands; note it in plan 16.
- **Seeds:** `--seeds K` (default 50) independent runs from a fresh save; median and 10th percentile of games per player; the strong-player bound = minimum over seeds of `strong`.
- **Python side** (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`, `report --simulate`): builds the matrix, calls `node authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts` once per cell (or once with all cells), prints the table, then the target check.
  - Flags: `--locale L` (default: every launch language; a locale without a pool file prints "no pool" and counts as fail), `--bundles a,b` (default: the default bundle set per locale; until RG-5 decides it: every bundle on for `es`, `base` only elsewhere), `--age-group G` (default all four), `--mode M` (default `solo`; `all` = the four non-gamemaster modes), `--players N` (default 1; multiplayer modes default 4), `--seeds K`, `--player strong|typical|both` (default both), `--json`.
  - Output per cell (locale × bundles × mode × age group): median, p10, strong bound, bottleneck level + difficulty + top 3 dry subcategories.
  - **Target check (pass/fail, D-75):** per launch language, approved count in that locale''s pool vs `authoring/data/targets.json` (`base` total 5000 and per difficulty). Per-locale targets come later from part 9; until then the `base` targets apply to every locale. ✓/✗ per locale, exit 1 on any ✗. The games numbers never change the exit code.
  - Speed: under ~1 min for the default matrix on today''s pool. If it''s slower, lower the default seeds rather than adding a cache.
- **Docs:** AGENTS.md `qgen report` line gets `--simulate`. In plan 16 "Metric": the player models, the joker policy, the mode approximations, and "pass/fail = D-75''s count".

## Tasks (to create)
1. `authoring/tools/sim/load.ts` + `simulate.ts` for `solo`/`rr-coop`, `strong` and `typical`, seeds, bottleneck; a throw-away check on today''s pool (D-76 says adults ≈ 8 games per player: the result should agree roughly). Priority 570.
2. Multiplayer models: `rr-competitive` and `timed` as above, `--players`. Priority 560.
3. `qgen report --simulate` in `qgen.py`: flags, matrix, table, `--json`, target check with exit code; AGENTS.md line; plan 16 CT-2 `[x]` with a note, "Metric" updated, `plans/project.md` in sync. Priority 550.

## Depends on / feeds
- Uses: engine (plans 19/20, done enough), age groups + bundle filter (plan 27, in `resolveChoice`), per-locale pools (part 3, task 242: missing pools print "no pool"), the default bundle set per language (part 10, task 249, RG-5: provisional default above), plan 51 (PORT-8: shares `load.ts`).
- Feeds: part 9 (task 248: bottlenecks → targets per locale), part 12 (task 251: the exit check).
- Out of scope: `gamemaster` mode, a games-per-player bar (D-75), Steam language detection.', '2026-10-12T17:55:28Z', 240);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (63, 9, 'Translation layout and schema (QT-1, I18N-3)', 890, 'Part 3 of the masterplan (plan 9): the storage layout and schema for translated questions (QT-1, `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Storage") and the I18N-3 schema (`plans/15-i18n.md`). Launch languages are `es`, `en`, `de` (D-78, pm decision 26); `es` stays the source. This plan only defines files, fields, `qgen validate` and `qgen export`; it writes no translations of questions. The pipeline that fills the files is part 4 (task 244), the review view part 5 (task 245), the game side part 6 (task 246).

## Decisions this builds on
- D-78: `es`, `en`, `de` at launch; later `zh-Hans`, `ru`, `pt-BR` (milestone 12, on hold). `base` in es-419; no `es-ES` question variant (it is UI only, LUI-5).
- D-35: `app/` never reads `authoring/`; the export writes everything the game needs to `app/data/`.
- D-36: questions only through `qgen batch`; workers never edit pools by hand.
- D-39, D-43: regions are bundles; `region` on questions (old I18N-3 wording) is `bundle`, done. Base categories in `app/data/categories.json`, a bundle''s in `app/data/bundles/<id>/categories.json`; questions store `subcategory` (its Spanish name) and `bundle`.
- Plan 26 (licence fields): done; translated files carry no media fields, media stays on the source.
- Plan 62: `qgen report --simulate` and `authoring/tools/sim/load.ts` already read `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` (es falls back to `pool.json`). This plan makes those files exist.

## Layout (preference A of 15b, recorded as a D-entry)
- `authoring/data/questions.json`: unchanged, the Spanish source.
- `authoring/data/questions.<locale>.json` per translated locale (`en`, `de`): `{"version": 1, "locale": "en", "questions": [...]}`, entries sorted by id, same ids as the source.
- Entry fields:
  - `id` (source id), `source_hash`, `status` (`draft` | `needs_work` | `approved` | `rejected`, as the source), `difficulty` (own, D-38 scale, rated for that language''s main market), `batch`, `review` (same shape as the source''s).
  - Translated text: `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers`, `hints`, `description`, `fun_fact`.
  - Nothing else from the source: `subcategory`, `bundle`, `media`, `background`, `concept`, `axes` are read from the source by id. Part 4/5 may add their own pipeline fields (e.g. a media-text flag) through the module below.
- `source_hash`: first 12 hex of sha256 over the canonical JSON of the source''s text fields (`question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers`, `hints`, `description`, `fun_fact`). Written when the translation is made.
- **`stale` is derived, not stored:** hash ≠ the source''s current hash. A stale translation is left out of the export (a fixed Spanish answer must not ship a wrong translated one) until part 4 re-translates it; `validate` counts them per locale (warning). Note in 15b: whole-pool rewrites (`qgen tighten`, neutral Spanish, part 8) stale every touched translation, hence full runs after milestone 1 (masterplan order).
- **`translatable: false`** on a source question (absent = translatable): wordplay, questions about Spanish itself, answers only Colombians know. Set by part 4''s translate step through review; `validate` accepts the field on any status.

## Translated names
- Subcategory names stay the Spanish keys everywhere (pool, burns, engine); a locale only adds display names.
- `app/data/names.<locale>.json`: `{"version": 1, "locale": "en", "bundles": {"<id>": {"name": …, "description": …}}, "categories": {"<slug>": …}, "subcategories": {"<Spanish name>": …}}` for `base` and every bundle''s name/description (`bundles.json` is global).
- `app/data/bundles/<id>/names.<locale>.json`: the bundle''s own categories and subcategories, same shape without `bundles`. Mirrors the `categories.json` layout (D-43), so a pack ships its names with it.
- Hand-maintained files (they ship, like `categories.json`); not questions, so D-36 doesn''t apply. First drafts for `en`, `de` by a worker task here; the native speakers check them with part 11''s pilot spot check. New subcategories (plan 14) get names when their first translated question needs them (validate below).

## Code
- New `authoring/tools/translations.py`: `LOCALES` (`en`, `de`, D-78; the later ones added when milestone 12 resumes), `path(locale)`, `load(locale)` (empty when the file is missing), `save(locale, doc)` (sorted, same JSON style as `questions.json`), `source_hash(q)`, `is_stale(t, q)`, `play_entries(locale, source_pool)`. The one place part 4 (pipeline), part 5 (review) and the export read translations.
- `app/server/categories.py` (or the module that loads names for authoring): `load_names(locale)` merging base and bundle name files.
- `layout.py`: paths for the locale files and names files.

## `qgen export`
- Writes `app/data/pool.json` exactly as today (the current game, D-59).
- Per locale in `LOCALES` with a translation file: `app/data/pool.<locale>.json`, same version and shape as `pool.json`. An entry = the source''s play fields (`id`, `subcategory`, `bundle`, `media`, `background`) + the translation''s text fields and `difficulty`, `status: approved`. Included only when source approved, source translatable, translation approved, not stale.
- No `pool.es.json` (plan 62''s fallback stays). Names files are source files in `app/data/`, not exported.
- Prints the count per locale and stale/left-out counts.

## `qgen validate`
- Per locale file: header `locale` matches the file name and is in `LOCALES`; unique ids, every id in the source; status valid; `difficulty` on the scale; required text fields per status (as the source''s checks: three wrong answers, three hints, answer not among wrong answers, …; share the per-question text check instead of copying it).
- Error: a non-rejected translation of a `translatable: false` or `rejected` source.
- Warning: stale translations (count + first ids), approved translations whose source is no longer approved.
- Names: error when `pool.<locale>.json` uses a subcategory, category or bundle without a name in that locale; warning for the other missing names (count); error for a name key that doesn''t exist in the categories/bundles files (renamed subcategory).
- Export staleness: fails when any `pool.<locale>.json` differs from what `export` would write (as `pool.json` today), and when a `pool.<locale>.json` exists without a translation file.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. D-entry for the layout (this plan''s "Layout" and "Translated names"); `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Storage" decided → points to it, QT-1 schema part; `plans/15-i18n.md` I18N-3: `region` = `bundle` (D-39), translation layout → the D-entry; `directory.md` new paths. Priority 900.
2. `translations.py`, `layout.py` paths, `load_names`; `qgen export` per locale; `qgen validate` checks above. Verify with a throw-away locale file of 3 entries in a temp copy (fresh, stale, non-translatable source), no committed test. Priority 890.
3. Draft `app/data/names.en.json`, `names.de.json`, `app/data/bundles/colombia/names.{en,de}.json` for every current category, subcategory and bundle; `qgen validate` clean. Priority 880.

## Done when
- `qgen validate` and `qgen export` pass on the real repo with no translation files (nothing changes for `es`) and with a throw-away locale file.
- QT-1 `[x]` in 15b (schema part; `validate` covers translations and `stale`), I18N-3 `[x]` in 15; the D-entry in `plans/decisions.md`.

## Out of scope
- Translating questions (part 4, part 11), the review view (part 5), loading `pool.<locale>.json` and names in the game and the language setting (part 6).
- Whether a translated pool counts toward a language''s 5000 (D-75/D-78 leave it open; part 9/12). `qgen report --simulate` already counts what `pool.<locale>.json` holds.', '2026-10-12T18:13:37Z', 242);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (64, 9, 'Spanish variety (neutral Spanish)', 690, 'Part 8 of the masterplan (plan 9): rewrite `base` from Colombian usage into neutral Latin American Spanish (`es-419`) through the pipeline, and make every new `base` question come out neutral, while `colombia` keeps its Colombian voice (D-78, B-13). This plan builds the tools and prompts; the runs belong to part 11 "Release content runs" (plan task 250). Owner: `plans/15-i18n.md` ("Spanish varieties").

## Context
- D-78 (pm decision 27): `base` in `es-419`; the ~40 Colombianisms ("bombillo", "crispetas", "gripa", "arquero", "tinto") are rewritten through the pipeline (D-36); an `es-ES` variant only where the wording differs (regionalisms, `vosotros` in the UI); `colombia` stays Colombian; no finer variants.
- Today `authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md` says "Spanish, with Colombian usage" and "numbers the Colombian way" for every bundle, so each new `base` batch adds more Colombianisms. Fix the prompts first, or the rewrite never finishes.
- Closest existing tool: `qgen tighten` (`cmd_tighten`, `cmd_scan`, `prompts/tighten.md`): a whole-pool scan → fix → review 1 → research → review 2 → record → export → sync. A one-off rewrite of existing questions is that pattern, not a drafting batch, so this is its own command (`qgen neutralize`) like `tighten`, not a `qgen batch` flag.
- D-81: rewriting the source text stales the touched translations (`source_hash`), so full translation runs (QT-6) come after the neutralize run (part 11''s order).
- D-56/D-79: every run that changes approved questions gets an LLM audit and a blind spot check; the review tool already takes `run=<name>&sample=1` (plan 57).
- The UI''s `es-ES` override is LUI-5 (part 7), not this plan.

## Tasks
1. **Prompts: neutral voice per bundle + neutralize prompt (pm decision)** (priority 700, first)
   - `house-style.md` "Language": voice by bundle (`base`: neutral Latin American Spanish, words understood across Latin America and Spain where one exists; `colombia`: today''s Colombian usage list). The bundle''s voice is picked by code (like `{players}`), e.g. a `voice` string per bundle in `app/data/bundles.json` or a `{voice}` section filled in `prompt()`; the worker decides and notes it.
   - Number format for `base`: Colombian "2.640 / 42,195" vs. others; options in the decision.
   - `review.md`, `audit.md`: a `base` question in Colombian wording is `needs_work` (one line each).
   - New `prompts/neutralize.md` (scan task, like `tighten.md`): flag `base` questions whose wording (question, options, hints, description, fun_fact) uses Colombian or other national usage where a neutral word exists; `issue` names word → replacement. References anyone knows (Encanto, García Márquez) stay; Colombian content that needs a connection to Colombia is a bundle matter (D-49), not flagged here.
   - `es-ES` for questions: recommendation in the decision: no `questions.es-ES.json` at launch; neutral wording reads fine in Spain; the scan lists words with no pan-Hispanic form, so a sparse override can follow if there are many.
   - Ask with `pm decision add` (prompt diffs in the body; options: approve as drafted / changes), make the task''s follow-up pending on it. New prompts are the gamemaster''s (D-36).
2. **`qgen neutralize`** (waits for task 1''s decision)
   - `cmd_neutralize` modelled on `cmd_tighten`: run `neutralize-<n>`, resumes an open run; scan only `bundle == "base"`, approved + needs_work, chunks of 50, `prompts/neutralize.md`; then fix (with the issue) → media → sheets → review 1 → research → review 2 → record → audit (D-56, the run''s audit sample) → export → sync. Reuse `cmd_scan` with a prompt/filter parameter rather than a copy.
   - `--dry-run`: scan only, print flagged ids, issues and an estimated cost (from `costs.log` rates) before any fix.
   - Done line + exact `git add` like `tighten`; stale translation count per locale printed when locale files exist (D-81).
   - Verify with a throw-away script on a handful of known Colombianisms (grep `bombillo|crispetas|gripa`), no full run (that''s part 11).
3. **Docs: RUNBOOK, D-entry, QC**
   - `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`: `qgen neutralize` (no arguments) only when the gamemaster asks, same handling as `qgen tighten`.
   - `plans/decisions.md`: new D-entry "neutral Spanish rewrite via `qgen neutralize`" (amends D-36: one more gamemaster-asked command; the bundle voices); D-36 "related" line points to it.
   - `authoring/QC.md`: a neutralize run gets the same QC as a batch (`/review?run=neutralize-<n>&sample=1`, `qgen report --qc neutralize-<n>` if it reads runs; else note the gap in the backlog).
   - `AGENTS.md` "Pool" command list: `qgen neutralize`; `plans/15-i18n.md` "Spanish varieties" links this plan; `plans/backlog.md` B-13 → tooling done, runs in part 11; `plans/project.md` in sync.

## Done when
- New `base` drafts come out in `es-419`, `colombia` drafts stay Colombian (prompts approved by the gamemaster).
- `qgen neutralize` runs end to end on the pool through review, audit and QC; RUNBOOK, D-entry and QC.md say how. The actual run is part 11''s.

## Out of scope
- Running the rewrite on the whole pool (part 11); the UI''s `es-ES` catalog (LUI-5, part 7); moving questions between bundles (D-49); finer Spanish variants (D-78).', '2026-10-12T18:20:34Z', 243);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (65, 8, 'Seen counters instead of burning; supply warning and exhausted subcategories', 600, 'Replaces burning (D-28) with a seen counter per question. Repeats become a fallback, not a dead end. The gamemaster decided this on 2026-10-12; it gets a new D-entry that supersedes D-28''s burn rules.

## Profile = save
- One save = one profile. On Steam that is one Steam user (`plan 10: masterplan` of milestone 10, part 4 «Steam Cloud saves»: a save per SteamID). Without Steam it is the local save (`state/game.json`, the desktop `save/…/game.json`).
- Player names stay labels: «Continuar: Sofía, nivel 5», game history, multiplayer turn order. They no longer scope selection; every seen event counts for the whole save, in every mode.
- GF-7 «Borrar jugador» deletes the name and its games but keeps their seen rows (the profile still saw those questions).

## Seen counter
- Events: the same ones that burn today (answered, skipped by joker or admin, swapped away, Snipe hit). Unpicked card descriptions don''t count.
- Save v3: `seen: {question_id, game_id, seen_on}[]` replaces `burned`; count(q) = rows for q. One row per event, so undo removes exactly that game''s row.
- `blocked: string[]`: «Saltar y quemar para todos» becomes «Bloquear pregunta», a hard exclusion for broken questions.
- Migration v2 → v3 in `parseSave` (fixtures, test on a copy of the family save): each `burned` row with `player_id` → one `seen` row (two kids who saw it = count 2); `player_id: null` → `blocked`.
- Python server (frozen, D-59): it only stores the document (D-67). Check that nothing in `app/server/` still reads `burned`; otherwise record the divergence.

## Selection
- `available`: approved, active bundles, not blocked, not offered this game, not purged. Seen questions are no longer excluded.
- `draw`: after the shuffle, sort by `(count, category key)`. The lowest count always wins; category variety only breaks ties. Then accept the first candidate that keeps the later levels fillable (as now). Jokers draw the same way.
- The hard supply-check failure stays only for "the whole pool, any count, can''t fill 12 levels".
- Engine tests: the invariant "burned never comes back" becomes "never a count-k card while a count-<k card fits the slot and keeps the later levels fillable".

## Low-supply warning (game start)
- After mode, bundles and age group are chosen, before level 1; informational, «Jugar» stays.
- Fresh games left k = the largest k such that the count-0 questions fill `4 + k·b` slots per level (`assign` with a per-level demand; binary search). `b` = seen events per level per game for the mode (D-75 multipliers: ≈ (12 + standard joker burns)/12; × N players in `rr-competitive` and `timed`).
- Warn when k < K. K is a pm decision for the gamemaster (proposal: 3).
- Bottleneck: the level(s) that fail first at k+1, shown as their difficulty range: «Quedan preguntas nuevas para unas 2 partidas; después se repetirán algunas, sobre todo de dificultad 13–15.» If a bundle is off, suggest switching it on. k = 0: «En esta partida pueden salir preguntas que ya vieron.»
- Strings in the `es` catalog (LUI-1); reachable with keys and pad.

## Exhausted subcategories (informational)
- A subcategory is exhausted when every approved question of it in the active bundles, within the age group''s overall difficulty span, has count ≥ 1.
- Shown at game start, once per subcategory: «Ya vieron todas las preguntas de: Ríos, Mundiales de fútbol». The save keeps `notified_exhausted`; a subcategory leaves the list when an update brings it unseen questions.
- No effect on selection.

## Also
- `qgen report --simulate` (CT-2): simulate with counts; "games until the first repeat" stays the headline; print k for a fresh profile as a cross-check.
- Docs: D-28 superseded in `plans/02`, `03`, `04`, `05`, `12`, `13`, `16`; `directory.md` if files move.', '2026-10-12T18:23:46Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (66, 9, 'Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)', 700, 'Part 4 of the masterplan (plan 9): the pipeline that fills `authoring/data/questions.<locale>.json` (D-81, plan 63) with translated, re-rated, fact-checked, reviewed and audited questions, started by one command, `qgen batch --translate <locale>` (D-36). Launch locales `en`, `de` (D-78). This plan builds the steps, prompts and entry point; the runs (pilot QT-5, full runs QT-6) belong to part 11 (plan task 250), the side-by-side review view to part 5 (task 245), cost and budget to part 9 (task 248). Owner: `plans/15b-question-translation.md` ("Pipeline"; QT-2, QT-3).

## Builds on
- D-81 / plan 63 (done): `authoring/tools/translations.py` (`LOCALES`, `load`, `save`, `source_hash`, `is_stale`, `translatable`, `plays`), `qgen export` → `app/data/pool.<locale>.json`, `qgen validate` per locale, names files. Translations carry only the text fields + own `difficulty`, `status`, `batch`, `review`, `source_hash`; media stays on the source.
- D-36: one command per job; workers never edit pools, prompts or media. D-55: health stop + `qgen health ack`. D-56/D-79: audit sample + blind spot check per run, agreement ≥ 90 % on ≥ 30.
- D-32/D-33: LLM review is a pipeline step, recorded as `reviewer: "llm"` + model. D-38: one difficulty scale 1–15.
- D-83 / plan 64: `qgen neutralize` stales touched translations; full runs come after it (part 11''s order). `cmd_neutralize` shows the pattern of a run mode reusing the batch steps (`run.json` `mode`, `run_steps`, report, "Commit exactly this").
- Existing steps all read the run''s drafts or `POOL`: `cmd_rate`, `cmd_factcheck`, `cmd_review`, `cmd_fix`, `cmd_record`, `cmd_audit`. Make them locale-aware through the run (`run.json` `locale`), not copies.

## Run
- `qgen batch --translate <locale>` (`locale` in `translations.LOCALES`): run `tr-<locale>-<n>` (e.g. `tr-en-1`); resumes an open run of that locale; `run.json` `{"mode": "translate", "locale", "ids", "started"}`. The run name is the translations'' `batch`.
- Steps: translate → rate → factcheck → merge → review 1 → fix → factcheck (changed facts, as `fix` does) → review 2 → record → audit → export → validate → batch-report. No concepts, draft, revise, media search or sheets.
- Selection (by code, D-36):
  - Sources: `approved`, translatable, bundle `base` (other bundles once RG-5, part 10, says which are translated per locale), no approved non-stale translation, not rejected in that locale.
  - Stale translations first (re-translated from the current source; the old entry''s review kept as `previous`).
  - Then subcategories with the fewest approved translations first, spread over the difficulty scale within each; ties in `categories.json` order.
  - Size: constant `TRANSLATE_SIZE` (proposal 300 sources). **Pilot:** the first run of a locale (no translation file yet) takes 50 (QT-5).
  - Hidden `--count`, `--ids` for tests/debugging only (like `qgen batch`).
- Stop after the pilot: the next `--translate <locale>` exits 2 until `qgen health ack tr-<locale>-1 "<note>"` (the gamemaster''s go after part 11''s pilot decision). Health thresholds (D-55) per translation run where they apply (needs_work and reject share, audit agreement); the worker picks the subset and notes it in `health.py`.
- Exit codes and usage-limit waiting as `qgen batch` (RUNBOOK step 3 unchanged).

## Steps
- **translate** (new `cmd_translate`, opus): chunks per subcategory (~15 questions), `prompts/translate.md` + house-style locale section. Input: source text fields, subcategory, difficulty, media role/type + the picked media''s title/description (to spot visible text). Output per id: translated `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers`, `hints`, `description`, `fun_fact`; `travels` (`yes` | `no` + reason: wordplay, about Spanish itself, needs Colombian knowledge); `media_text` (the media likely shows text in Spanish: bool); `notes` (adaptations made: units, answer format, hint rewritten). Writes `work/<run>/translations/<chunk>.json`.
- **rate --locale** (`cmd_rate` with the run''s locale): same `RATE_SCHEMA`, prompt = house-style + `rate.md` + a locale section: difficulty and distractors judged for the locale''s main market (D-38 scale); overlap candidates from that locale''s approved translations.
- **factcheck --locale** (`cmd_factcheck`): only items whose translation changed a number, unit, date or record vs. the source, or `needs_fact_check` on the source; the rest inherits the source''s check. Prompt in the target language''s framing ("Questions (English)").
- **merge**: entries into `questions.<locale>.json` with `status: draft`, `batch`, `source_hash` (of the source now), `difficulty` from the rating; `travels: no` → no entry, id listed in `work/<run>/not-travelling.json` for review.
- **review 1/2** (`cmd_review` with locale): payload = source (Spanish) + translation + rater notes + fact check + related translated questions + the source''s picked media (no search, no new pick); `prompts/review.md` + `translate-review.md` (fidelity, natural target language, adapted hints, distractors plausible in that language, `media_text`). `can_search_again: false`. Not-travelling ids get a one-line review too: confirm → `translatable: false`, else translated next run.
- **fix**: revise the translation once with the review''s `fix` (as QG-22), facts re-checked if changed.
- **record** (`cmd_record` with locale): writes `status`, `review` (D-33 shape), `media_text` into the locale file; the media rules of the source don''t apply; unconfirmed fact check → `needs_work`. Confirmed not-travelling → `translatable: false` on the source in `questions.json` (not a text field: no source staleness).
- **audit** (`cmd_audit` with locale): seeded sample of `AUDIT_SAMPLE` from the locale file, `audit.md` + the locale section, source shown alongside; findings → `work/<run>/audit/`, report''s Audit section.
- **batch-report**: `authoring/reports/tr-<locale>-<n>.md`: translated, approved, needs work, rejected, not travelling, `media_text` count, stale re-translated, cost per approved translation (`costs.log`, feeds part 9''s CT-3), audit; QC section by `qgen report --qc <run>`; spot-check link `/review?batch=<run>&locale=<locale>&sample=1` (part 5) for a native speaker.
- "Commit exactly this": `authoring/data/questions.<locale>.json`, `authoring/data/questions.json` (if `translatable` changed), `app/data/pool.<locale>.json`, the report.

## Prompts (new prompts are the gamemaster''s, D-36)
- New `prompts/translate.md`: adapt, don''t translate literally (units to the market, number format, answer format, idioms); keep the answer and the fact unchanged; three wrong answers plausible in the target language, never accidentally correct; hints that play on Spanish words rewritten to work in the target language; `description` humour adapted, not translated word by word; when it doesn''t travel, say so instead of forcing it.
- New `prompts/translate-review.md` (appended to `review.md` / `audit.md` for locale runs): what a translation review checks on top of D-32.
- House-style: a `{locale}` section filled by `prompt()` per locale: language, market and conventions (`en`: proposal US + UK families, US spelling, metric with imperial where natural; `de`: Germany, Austria, Switzerland, standard German, `ß` per Germany). Everything else in house-style stays (it is about questions, not Spanish), except the "Language" voice block, which applies to `es` only.
- Market per locale and the prompt texts: one pm decision (diffs in the body; options: approve as drafted / changes).

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Prompts and market per locale (pm decision)** (priority 710, first): draft `translate.md`, `translate-review.md`, the house-style locale section and the `{locale}` filling in `prompt()`; `pm decision add` with the drafts and the market proposal; make tasks 2–4 pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`). Stage only the drafts.
2. **Translate, rate, factcheck, merge per locale**: `cmd_translate` + `TRANSLATE_SCHEMA`; locale in `run.json` read by `cmd_rate`, `cmd_factcheck` (`drafts`/`collect` per mode); merge into the locale file through `translations.save`. Single steps callable for debugging (`qgen translate --run …`), like the other steps. Verify on a git worktree with `--ids` of 5 questions, `en`; discard.
3. **Review, fix, record, audit per locale**: `cmd_review`, `cmd_fix`, `cmd_record`, `cmd_audit`/`audit_input` read and write the locale file when the run has a locale; `translatable: false` path; `media_text`. Verify on the same worktree run.
4. **`qgen batch --translate L`**: `cmd_batch` branch (or `cmd_translate_batch`), selection rules, `TRANSLATE_SIZE`, pilot size 50, pilot stop via `health` (+ which thresholds apply), batch report, commit lines, `qgen report --qc` and `/stats` reading `tr-*` runs where they list batches (`health.batch_runs` stays `batch-*`). Verify one full run with `--count 5` on a worktree (≈$2); discard.
5. **Docs and D-entry**: D-entry "Translations through `qgen batch --translate`" (run names, selection, pilot stop, steps); D-36 "amended by"; `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` (only when the user names a language: `qgen batch --translate <locale>`; same exit codes; the pilot stop); `authoring/QC.md` (native-speaker spot check for `tr-*` runs); AGENTS.md command list; `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Pipeline" + QT-2, QT-3 `[x]`; `directory.md` (`work/tr-*`, new prompts). Priority 690.

## Done when
- `qgen batch --translate en` on a worktree with `--count 5` runs end to end: locale file written, `pool.en.json` exported, `qgen validate` clean, report written; no change to `es` (`pool.json` identical).
- Prompts approved by pm decision; RUNBOOK, D-36, D-entry, 15b updated.

## Out of scope
- Real runs: pilot (QT-5) and full runs (QT-6) are part 11; the go/no-go and budget are parts 11 and 9.
- The review view `&locale=` and its sample mode (part 5); the game loading `pool.<locale>.json` (part 6).
- Translating names files (plan 63, task 3); media with text replaced per locale (flagged only; a later backlog item if many).
- Which bundles are translated (RG-5, part 10); the later locales (milestone 12).', '2026-10-12T19:15:14Z', 244);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (67, 9, 'Review tool for translations (QT-4)', 400, 'Part 5 of the masterplan (plan 9): the authoring review tool and stats pages learn translations (QT-4, `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Review tool"). The gamemaster and native speakers review `authoring/data/questions.<locale>.json` (D-81, plan 63) with the Spanish source side by side, with the same verdicts, a per-locale "media shows text" flag and the blind spot-check sample of plan 16 per translation run. Launch locales `en`, `de` (decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31)). The pipeline that fills the files is plan 66 (`plan 66: Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)`); its batch report already links `/review?batch=tr-<locale>-<n>&locale=<locale>&sample=1`, which this plan makes work.

## Builds on
- D-81 / plan 63 (done): `authoring/tools/translations.py` (`LOCALES`, `load`, `save`, `is_stale`, `translatable`, `plays`, `exports`, `counts`); names in `app/data/names.<locale>.json` (+ per bundle), loader `load_names(locale)`.
- Plan 66 (tasks 438–440, open, pending on decision 35): runs `tr-<locale>-<n>` = the translations'' `batch`; `record` writes `status`, `review` (D-33 shape), `media_text` into the locale file and `work/<run>/recorded.json`; audit findings in `work/<run>/audit/<id>.json`; sample via `qgen.audit_sample(run)`. Build against these shapes; verify with throw-away files if 438–440 aren''t done yet.
- D-32/D-33: a human decision replaces the LLM review and keeps it as `previous`; undo restores. Plan 16 (task 47): sample mode, blind until decided, `authoring/data/spot-checks.json`, `authoring/server/spot_checks.py`.
- D-35/D-36: the review tool is the human''s way to change a pool; it re-exports after every change (here `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` via `translations.exports`).

## Server (`authoring/server/main.py`, `spot_checks.py`)
- `GET /api/questions?locale=<l>` (`l` in `LOCALES`; `es` or absent = today): one item per translation entry: the source question (id, `subcategory`, `bundle`, `media`, `background`, `translatable`, candidates) with the translation''s text fields, `difficulty`, `status`, `batch`, `review`, `media_text`, plus `source` (the Spanish text fields, `difficulty`, `status`) and `stale` (bool).
  - Filters: `batch`, `status`, `reviewer`, `sample`, `audit` on the translation; `bundle`, `subcategory`, `media` on the source. `stale=1` only stale ones.
  - `audit`: the translation''s own (`work/<t.batch>/audit/<id>.json`), never the source''s back-audit (`qgen.audit_of` takes the batch, or a locale-aware sibling).
- POST with `"locale"` in the body: `review`, `difficulty` write the locale file through `translations` (one lock, re-read, atomic save, then the locale export), same rules and undo as the source; `difficulty_original` likewise.
  - New `POST /api/questions/<id>/media-text` `{"locale", "media_text": bool}`.
  - New `POST /api/questions/<id>/translatable` `{"translatable": bool}`: sets the source''s flag (`false` = doesn''t travel; not a text field, no staleness, plan 63). With `false`, non-rejected translations of that id are rejected with feedback "no viaja" (validate''s rule, plan 63).
  - `media`, `media/search`, `bundle` refuse a locale (400): media and bundle live on the source; the Spanish view changes them.
- Spot checks: `record(batch, q, …)` accepts a translation run (`tr-*`): batch checked against the translation''s `batch`, the item gets `"locale"`; LLM decision from the run''s `recorded.json`. Same file, keyed by run name.
- Docstring API lines for every new parameter and route.

## Review page (`authoring/ui/src/review/`)
- `?locale=en|de`: header shows the locale; a locale switch (es · en · de) keeps the other params.
- Side by side: left the Spanish source (read-only, its difficulty and status), right the translation; fields aligned row by row (question, answer, wrong answers, hints, description, fun fact). A stale translation gets a banner and no approve (its source changed; the next `--translate` run redoes it).
- Subcategory and bundle shown with the locale''s names (`names.<locale>.json`) and the Spanish key.
- Same verdicts, feedback, problem toggles, difficulty, undo, keyboard keys as the Spanish view. Media: shown, not pickable; a "media shows text" toggle (`media_text`), and the source''s media link to `/review?id=<id>` for changing it.
- "Doesn''t travel" button: sets `translatable: false` (with confirm); a source with `translatable: false` shows it and allows undoing.
- Sample mode (`&sample=1`): blind as plan 16: LLM review, feedback, audit and translator notes hidden until decided; the source stays visible (fidelity is part of the check). Reveal + agree/disagree as today.
- Keep `Review.svelte` from growing: the source column as its own component (e.g. `SourcePanel.svelte`).

## Stats and start page
- `/stats/*?locale=<l>` (with `bundle`): approved, playing translations (`translations.plays`) with their own difficulty; categories/subcategories by the source, labelled with the locale''s names; targets as for Spanish (whether a translated pool counts toward the 5000 is part 9/12, plan 63). Locale switch next to the bundle switch.
- Start page (`overview.py`, `home/Home.svelte`): per locale a row: approved, needs_work, draft, rejected, stale, not translatable, untranslated approved translatable sources (`translations.counts` + source); the `tr-*` runs in the batch table, linking `/review?batch=…&locale=…` and the sample.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Server: locale in the question API** (priority 400): `GET /api/questions?locale=`, the POST routes with `locale`, `media-text`, `translatable`, locale export after each change, locale-aware `audit`, refusals; docstring. Verify with a throw-away `questions.en.json` of 3 entries (fresh, stale, non-translatable source) on a git worktree via `curl`; discard.
2. **Review page side by side** (priority 400): locale switch, source column, names, stale banner, verdicts/difficulty/undo, `media_text` toggle, doesn''t travel. `npm run check`, `npm run build`; click through on the worktree file from task 1.
3. **Spot check per locale** (priority 400): `spot_checks.record` for `tr-*` runs, `locale` on items, blind sample mode in the locale view; `qgen validate`''s spot-check check accepts `tr-*` items. Verify with a fake `work/tr-en-1/` (`run.json`, `recorded.json`, an audit file) on the worktree; discard.
4. **Stats and start page per locale** (priority 390).
5. **Docs** (priority 380): `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Review tool" (what exists) and QT-4 `[x]`; `plans/08-review-tool.md` new RV entries (locale view, spot check per locale); `directory.md` if files were added; `authoring/QC.md`: the native speaker''s spot check link and steps for `tr-*` runs, if task 441 didn''t write them already.

## Done when
- On a worktree with a throw-away locale file: `/review?locale=en` shows source and translation side by side; a decision, a difficulty change, `media_text` and doesn''t-travel write the locale file and `app/data/pool.en.json`; undo restores; `qgen validate` clean.
- `/review?batch=tr-en-1&locale=en&sample=1` is blind and records into `spot-checks.json`; `/stats/difficulty?locale=en` and the start page show the locale.
- The Spanish view and `pool.json` unchanged (D-59).

## Out of scope
- The pipeline and its runs (plan 66, part 11); finding native speakers (the gamemaster).
- Replacing media with visible text per locale (flagged only; backlog if many, plan 66).
- Flags from a game played in English/German (`apply_flags` with a locale): part 6 (task 246) decides how flags carry the locale.
- Reworking needs_work translations: the next `--translate` run picks them again (plan 66''s selection).', '2026-10-12T19:34:03Z', 245);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (68, 9, 'Language setting and per-locale pool (I18N-2)', 480, 'Part 6 of the masterplan (plan 9): the player picks the UI language and the question language; the game plays from that locale''s pool and shows that locale''s category and bundle names; a fresh save asks for the language once, on first start (milestone 9''s revision; replaces this plan''s earlier "no first-start language screen"). Launch languages `es`, `en`, `de` (D-78, decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31)); `es-ES` is a UI variant only (decision 27: Spanish variety). Owner: `plans/15-i18n.md` "Model", I18N-2. The family''s game stays as today: Spanish, gamemaster mode unchanged (D-59).

## Builds on
- Plan 63 (done, D-81): `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` (no `pool.es.json`: `es` = `pool.json`), `app/data/names.<locale>.json`, `app/data/bundles/<id>/names.<locale>.json`; subcategory keys stay Spanish everywhere.
- Plan 65 (seen counters, supersedes D-28''s burns): `seen` rows by question id for the whole save. Ids are shared across locales, so switching languages never repeats a question with no extra work; the outlook and the low-supply warning (decision 31: super-tight) run on the loaded locale''s pool.
- Catalog (plan 21, D-70): `lib/i18n.ts`, `CATALOGS`, `?lang=` dev override. `en` draft: plan 24; `de`, `es-ES`: plan 69. This plan only switches between whatever catalogs exist.
- Plan 36 has no general settings screen (only the mode screen, MD-7); plan 59 grows the overlay into the gamemaster menu.
- Decision 4 (Python server: static + `/api/save`): new save fields pass through untouched; `/data/` serves the new files statically.
- Built (tasks 449, 450): `SaveData.language`, `GameRow.locale` (decision 36: written only for non-es games), `defaultLanguage()` in `engine/save.ts`, `ready()`/`language()` in `lib/engine.ts`, boot language in `main.ts`, Esc menu rows in `Overlay.svelte`, `displayName`.

## Decisions taken here
- **Save field, no version bump**: `SaveData.language?: { ui: string; questions: string }`. A stored save without it = `{ui: "es", questions: "es"}` (`parseSave`), so the family''s save and fixtures stay Spanish whatever the browser says. A fresh save (`emptySave()`: no file, 404, or a backed-up broken file) gets the default below. Profile = save (plan 65): on Steam it travels with the SteamID''s save.
- **Default for a fresh save**: best match of the guessed tag among the existing catalogs (UI) and locales with a pool (questions): exact tag, then the language part (`es-CO` → `es`, `de-AT` → `de`, `es-ES` → `es-ES` UI + `es` questions), else `en` if present, else `es`. Guessed tag: `navigator.language` now; Steam''s client language once milestone 10 provides it (one seam, `guessTag()`; not wired here).
- **A game keeps its locale**: `GameRow.locale?` (missing = `es`), set by `newGame` from `language.questions`. Continuing a game loads its own locale''s data; a language change applies to the next game. No mid-game pool swap.
- **Esc menu**: two rows «Idioma» / «Idioma de las preguntas» in every mode (next to sound), shown only with ≥2 options. Today (only `es` catalog, only `pool.json`) nothing appears.
- **First-start language screen** (milestone 9):
  - Shown when the loaded save is fresh (no `language` stored, i.e. `emptySave()`), before the start screen; asked once: confirming writes `language`, so it never shows again. A stored save without `language` (the family''s) is parsed as `es` and never sees it.
  - Skipped while there is nothing to pick (one UI option and one question locale, as today); nothing is written then, so it asks once a second language ships.
  - One list of UI languages by endonym (same data as the Esc rows), the guess preselected and focused; confirm = Enter / pad A / click. A pick sets both: `ui` = the pick, `questions` = `defaultLanguage(pick)` over the locales whose supply check passes for the default bundles (`es` always). Separate question language: Esc menu.
  - No `t()` text needed to choose: endonyms plus a heading and a confirm prompt in the guessed UI language (`language.*` keys).
  - Confirm with a different UI language than the boot one: save, then `location.reload()` (same rule as the Esc menu); same one: continue to the start screen without reload.
- **Options**: UI = catalogs in `CATALOGS` minus `xx`; questions = locales whose pool file exists (`es` always). A question locale whose pool fails the supply check for the default bundles is listed but disabled in the Esc menu, with the reason.
- **UI language change reloads the app**; `lang` stays a module constant set once at boot. No reactive catalog.
- **Names**: `displayName(kind, key)` from the loaded locale''s names files; fallback the Spanish key/`categories.json` name.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Engine and data** (task 449, done).
2. **UI: Esc menu rows, names, boot** (task 450, done).
3. **Docs** (task 451; runs after task 4): the D-entry and `plans/15-i18n.md` "Model" also cover the first-start screen; `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` gets the screen next to the Esc menu rows.
4. **First-start language screen** (priority 470, before the docs task)
   - `lib/engine.ts`: `ready()` remembers whether the stored save had no `language` (fresh); `language()` returns `ask: boolean` (fresh and >1 UI option or >1 question locale). `guessTag()` wraps `navigator.language` (the seam for milestone 10).
   - `Game.svelte`: a `language` screen before `start` when `ask`; a new component (e.g. `game/LanguageScreen.svelte`): the endonym list, guess preselected, action layer scope and `data-nav` (IN-2..IN-5), keys and pad; confirm → `setLanguage` → reload if `ui` changed, else `start`. Esc menu not reachable on this screen (nothing to configure yet).
   - Strings via `t()` (`language.choose`, `language.confirm` or similar) in `es` and in whatever other catalogs exist (plan 24''s `en` if present, else noted for plan 69); `npm run check:literals`.
   - Check: `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `npm test`; throw-away: browser walk with no save file and throw-away `pool.en.json` + `names.en.json` + a stub `en` catalog: `navigator.language` `de-AT` → `en` preselected; pick `Español (Latinoamérica)` → reload, Spanish start screen; reload again → no screen; a copy of the family save → no screen; only `es` present → no screen, nothing written; keyboard only, pad.

## Done when
- The family''s save plays exactly as today (fixture replay passes, no language rows or screen with only `es`; never a screen for a stored save).
- With a second pool and catalog present: a fresh save opens on the language screen with the guessed language preselected, asks once; a player switches both languages from the Esc menu; the next game draws from that locale''s pool with its names, never repeating a question seen in another language before unseen ones run out.

## Out of scope
- Catalogs `en`, `de`, `es-ES` (plans 24, 69), translated pools (plans 66, part 11), Steam client language (milestone 10 wires it into `guessTag()`), store page (LUI-6).', '2026-10-12T19:36:15Z', 246);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (69, 9, 'UI catalogs for the launch languages (LUI-4, LUI-5)', 370, 'Part 7 of the masterplan (plan 9): every screen of the game in the launch languages, checked by native speakers. Launch catalogs `es` (neutral Latin American, es-419), `es-ES` (override), `en`, `de` (D-78; decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31); decision 27: Spanish variety (OQ-31)). Owner: `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` (LUI-4, LUI-5). The family''s game stays Spanish with today''s keys (D-59), unless the LUI-4 decision says otherwise.

## Builds on
- Plan 21 (done, D-70): `lib/i18n.ts`, `locales/es.ts`, `Catalog`/`Key` types, `npm run check:literals -w app/client`.
- Plan 23 (LUI-2): `xx` pseudo-locale, its screen walk and backlog rows (origin `LUI-2`). Plan 24 (LUI-3): draft `en.ts`, English joker name decisions, rows (origin `LUI-3`). Both at 400, before this plan; a task here that needs `xx.ts` or `en.ts` and finds it missing stops with a note.
- Plan 68 (I18N-2): language rows in the Esc menu, boot language from the save, endonyms «Español (España)», «Deutsch»; first-start language screen (task 490, milestone 9 revision) with its `language.*` keys in `es` (and `en` if present). It switches between whatever is in `CATALOGS`; this plan fills it, so the screen first appears once a second catalog ships here.
- Plan 45 (done): `Prompt.svelte`, `Glyph.svelte`, `KEY_LABELS` in `lib/input.svelte.ts`. Pad glyphs are language-independent; only key letters and text labels vary.
- Plan 46 (SW-4, 380, before this plan): `LetterPicker.svelte` with Spanish letters (`Ñ Á É Í Ó Ú Ü`); task 3 stops with a note if it doesn''t exist yet.
- Plan 64 (neutral Spanish for questions); this plan does the UI side of D-78 (`es.ts` neutral, `es-ES` override).

## Design
- **Shipping catalogs**: `CATALOGS` = `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`, statically imported (a few KB each; no lazy loading); `xx` stays dev-only. `en.ts`/`de.ts`: `satisfies Catalog`. `es-ES.ts`: `DeepPartial<Catalog>`, only differing leaves (`vosotros` for plural addressing, regionalisms), merged over `es` at boot; plural maps and variant arrays replaced whole, not merged per item.
- **Keys (LUI-4, pm decision)**: recommendation: keep keys in the catalog per language (`joker.<id>.key`, `flag.key`, `screen.question.replayKey`, `screen.start.newKey`), mnemonic for the name. `es` unchanged. Reasons: `toIntent` matches `e.key`, so letters work on QWERTZ/AZERTY, while position-based neutral keys (`Q W E R T`) don''t; `F1`–`F5` are awkward on laptops and the Deck; pads use focus anyway (decision 9). Rule per catalog, checked by `check:literals`: keys unique, single letter, not `A`–`D` (answers), not a digit, not a key of another scope on the same screen. Alternative options in the decision: neutral `1`–`5` row… (conflicts with `pick n`), `F1`–`F5`.
- **Joker names (like plan 24)**: playful German names, not literal translations; one pm decision per joker (`hint`, `skip`, `easier`, `category`, `snipe`), 3–5 candidates each, recommended first, ≤ «Francotirador»''s length. `es-ES` keeps the Spanish names unless a candidate reads off in Spain (then a decision).
- **First-start language screen**: its `language.*` keys (heading, confirm prompt) in every catalog; the guessed language''s catalog shows them, so each must read right on its own. Endonyms stay in plan 68''s data, not in catalogs.
- **Mode names**: English first (D-74); `de` drafted in the catalog, checked in the playtest; no separate decision.
- **`es` neutral**: scan `es.ts` for Colombian wording (copy lines, error texts). Family-visible, so changes go through one pm decision (list old → new); none applied before it.
- **Letter picker**: letters per UI language from the catalog (`picker.letters`): `es`/`es-ES` today''s set, `de` adds `Ä Ö Ü ß`, `en` `A`–`Z` + `-`.
- **Fonts**: Baloo 2 and Nunito (`app/client/public/fonts`) must have every character of every catalog (`ÄÖÜäöüß „“ ‚‘ – … ¡¿ «» ñ`). Checked once by a throw-away script (`nix shell nixpkgs#python3Packages.fonttools`); a gap → pm decision (other subset of the same family, OFL), not a new font silently. Latin only at launch (15a).
