7. **Review the UI shell, lib and configs; close the part: `App.svelte`, `main.ts`, `app.css`, `index.html`, `lib/Nav.svelte`, `lib/api.ts`, `lib/types.ts`, `package.json`, `vite.config.ts`, `svelte.config.js`, `tsconfig.json`, `.gitignore`** (25 + 5 + 27 + 12 + 34 + 102 + 215 + 18 + 18 + 3 + 31 + 2 lines)
   - `lib/types.ts` vs. the server''s actual JSON (run the temp server once, compare a response of every route to the types: missing, extra, optional fields), types never used; `lib/api.ts`: error handling (non-2xx, JSON parse), one helper vs. copy-pasted `fetch`es, routes vs. `main.py`''s docstring.
   - `App.svelte` routing (unknown path), `Nav.svelte` links vs. routes; `vite.config.ts` proxy/port and `$app` alias, `tsconfig.json` strictness vs. `app/client` (difference → part 10 row), `package.json` deps vs. imports.
   - Close: `git ls-files authoring/server authoring/ui` vs. the part 1 inventory and tasks 1–7; files added since (e.g. `SourcePanel.svelte` from task 444) reviewed with the same checklist and added to the inventory with part 9 (if that exceeds this run: `pm task add <this plan>` per remaining group); this part''s duplication candidates collected in one list in `## Part 9` for part 10.

## Done when
- Every tracked file of `authoring/server/` and `authoring/ui/` at the time of task 7 is listed in `## Part 9` (no-findings rows included) and in the inventory, every finding with a status; every part 1 row `handed to part 9` has its final status there.
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-12T22:59:31Z', 510);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (82, 13, 'Cross-cutting duplication, consistency and build config (code review part 10)', 0, 'Part 10 of `plan 72: masterplan` (milestone 13, Code quality): consolidate the duplication candidates found by parts 2–9, check naming and error handling across files, review the build/package config, and check `directory.md`/`AGENTS.md`/`README.md` against the code last; fix what is cheap, log every file and finding in `## Part 10` of `code-review.md`. Scope, checklist, fix-or-ask, the task 302 rule, duplication candidates and the report format: plan 72 "Ground rules for every part"; not restated here.

## Depends on
- Parts 1–9 (plans 73–81): runs after them (same priority 0, higher plan id). **Every task re-reads `code-review.md`** (rows "duplication candidate", rows `handed to part 10`, follow-up tasks and decisions already opened) rather than assuming the clusters below; the lists here are what plans 74–81 announced, not what they found.
- Every part 1 row `handed to part 10` gets its final status in `## Part 10`, quoting the part 1 row; every duplication candidate row of parts 2–9 gets one status there too (consolidated / `follow-up task N` / `decision N` / `superseded by task N` / `won''t fix: <why>`, e.g. two languages on purpose).
- Open work elsewhere (first step of every task: `pm show <id>`, `pm queue`): `task 302: Delete the Python referee` (plan 51, pending decision 25) deletes `game.py`, `selection.py`, `flags.py`, `record_fixtures.py` → Python ↔ TS port duplication is `superseded by task 302`; plans 53, 67, 30 (tasks 309/310, 443–446, 477) still touching authoring files → findings only, no conflicting refactor.
- Binding: decision 4 (game server routes), decision 5 (supply via the TS engine under Node), decision 12 (desktop shell), D-59 (save read-only for authoring), D-71/D-72 (`app://`, desktop save), D-73 (local builds; CI is local per AGENTS.md), D-70 (typed catalog), AGENTS.md "Layout" (`authoring/` may import `app/`, never the reverse; `app/` never reads `authoring/data/`). `pm decision list --answered --grep <term>` before each consolidation.

## Rules for this plan
- Consolidate only where it is local and behaviour-neutral: one source of truth inside one language and one side of the layout rule (e.g. `authoring/ui` importing a type from `$app/lib/types.ts` instead of a copy). Cross-language duplication (Python ↔ TS/Node: save envelope, cache file names, MIME/range, path roots) is not merged by code: options are a shared JSON constant file, a parity check in an existing test, or "won''t fix, documented" → `pm decision add` (recommended first) + follow-up task via `pm task-pending-decision` when it changes structure or a format.
- Formats unchanged without a decision: save envelope, pool JSON, `app/data/pool*.json` byte-identical after `qgen export`, media cache file names, API routes/JSON shapes, URLs, CLI flags.
- Build config changes: `nix flake check` is not required, but `nix develop -c true` and `nix build .#app` (update `npmDepsHash` if the lockfile changes) when `flake.nix`, `flake.lock`, `package.json` or `package-lock.json` change; `trivia-desktop-build` only when `app/desktop` packaging is affected (part 6 owns it; note why if skipped). No new dependencies (AGENTS.md); removing unused ones is in scope.
- Real `state/`, `authoring/data/`, `work/`, media cache are never written: servers and scripts on temp `TRIVIA_STATE`/`TRIVIA_MEDIA`/`TRIVIA_WORK`.
- A cluster too big for its task: fix the cheap part, `pm task add <this plan>` per remaining piece with exact files.
- Before every commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.

## Tasks (in this order; no own priority)
1. **Triage: one duplication table for part 10**
   - Collect every "duplication candidate" row of parts 2–9 and every `handed to part 10` row of part 1 into `### Duplication clusters` in `## Part 10`: one row per cluster (all paths), source rows quoted by part, assigned to task 2–6 below (or `superseded by task 302`, or a new follow-up task if it fits none).
   - Candidates no part logged but plan 72 names (the two `types.ts`, the two `api.ts`, chart/CSS copies): grep once, add if real.
   - No code changes; output is the table the next tasks work from.
2. **Client types and API clients** (`app/client/src/lib/types.ts` 173, `engine/state.ts` 273, `authoring/ui/src/lib/types.ts` 215; `lib/api.ts` 156, `engine/api.ts` 133, `authoring/ui/src/lib/api.ts` 102; `lib/store.ts` 116, `engine/store.ts` 26; `GameError` in `lib/api.ts` ↔ `engine/state.ts`)
   - Which types are the same shape (pool question, media, categories) → one definition, the copy imports it (authoring → `$app`, never the reverse); types that only look alike stay, row says why.
   - Fetch/error helpers: one `request`/error mapping per side or shared from `$app/lib`; locale lists (`lib/data.ts` `LOCALES`, `i18n.ts` `CATALOGS`/`UI_LANGS`) vs. authoring locale lists, if logged.
   - Check: `npm run check`, `npm run build`, bundle sizes of both `dist`s vs. part 1''s baseline (importing from `$app` must not pull game code into the authoring bundle).
3. **Python ↔ Node/TS twins: save, paths, media cache, static serving** (`app/server/save.py` 109, `app/desktop/save.mjs` 92, `authoring/tools/save_file.py` 85, `engine/save.ts` 78; `app/server/paths.py` 33, `authoring/tools/layout.py` 38, desktop `REPO`/roots; `app/server/media_cache.py` 32, `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` 129, `authoring/tools/download.py`/`media.py` `cmd_sync`; `app/server/http_base.py` 54 ↔ desktop `MIME`/`parseRange`/`sendFile`; `app/server/main.py` ↔ `authoring/server/main.py` handlers)
   - Inside Python: `paths.py` ↔ `layout.py` and `save.py` ↔ `save_file.py` may merge (authoring importing `app/server`, allowed) if task 302''s planned changes to them don''t conflict; otherwise follow-up task.
   - Across languages: list each rule that must stay identical (cache name hash/extension, envelope fields, atomic write, MIME table) and whether a mismatch exists today (throw-away script: same URL → same cache name in Python and Node; same save accepted by all three readers); mismatch = bug row + fix or task; keeping them in sync → decision with options per rule above.
4. **Authoring tools'' shared logic and constant copies** (after part 7''s module-structure decision, if any: read it first; `qgen.py` ↔ `health.py`, `translations.py`, `pool_export.py`, `targets.py`, `batches.py`, `authoring/server/overview.py`, `spot_checks.py`, `media_stats.py` ↔ `media.py`; `providers/*` rate limiting/`available()` ↔ `download.py`)
   - Constant copies: `LANGUAGES`/`LAUNCH_LOCALES`/`translations.LOCALES`, `SIM_MODES` (qgen ↔ `sim/simulate.ts`), `AGE_GROUP_IDS` ↔ `age_groups.json` (D-74/D-76), saturation/health thresholds: one owner module, the rest import it (TS ↔ Python copies: read from the JSON both already load, or decision).
   - Logic copies (report metrics ↔ `health.py`, `audit_of`, `batch_rows`, export paths): merge the small ones; a qgen split already decided by part 7 owns the big ones (don''t duplicate its follow-up tasks).
   - Check: `qgen validate`, `qgen report` and `qgen export` output identical before/after (diff, temp work dir), authoring server routes diffed with `curl` on a temp copy.
5. **Styles and screen helpers** (`app/client/src/game/theme.css`, `app/client/src/app.css`, component `<style>`s logged by part 5; `authoring/ui/src/app.css`, `stats/chart.css`; animation helpers in `Fireworks`/`Shredder`/`JokerFlight`; phase/copy logic in `Game.svelte`/`Overlay.svelte`/`Hud.svelte`/`copy.ts`)
   - Repeated colours/sizes → existing CSS variables of `theme.css`; authoring reuses `theme.css` variables where it already imports it (`print/JokerCards.svelte`), no new shared stylesheet unless clearly smaller.
   - Helpers repeated in three or more places → one module in `game/`; two places only if identical.
   - Check: decision 6 method (throw-away Playwright, before/after pixel diff of the touched screens) for any CSS change; `npm run check:literals -w app/client`.
6. **Consistency across files: naming, errors, env vars, ports**
   - Error handling: JSON error shape and status codes of `app/server` vs. `authoring/server`, client error codes (`lib/errors.ts`) vs. what servers/engine emit, Python `print`/`sys.exit`/logging and exception style across `app/server`, `authoring/server`, `authoring/tools`; Node `main.mjs`/`save.mjs` errors.
   - Naming: file names (snake vs. kebab vs. camel per language), Spanish vs. English identifiers, `TRIVIA_*` env vars (every one read in code is documented in `README.md`/`directory.md`, none documented but unread), ports `8000`/`8001`/`5174` repeated in servers, `vite.config.ts`s, `flake.nix`, README.
   - `PLACEHOLDER(<id>)` format and AGENTS.md comment rules (part 1 scan rows re-checked for the files of no other part).
   - Small renames inside one file → fix; renames across files or env vars/ports (behaviour/format) → decision + follow-up task.
7. **Build and package config** (`flake.nix` 130, `flake.lock`, root `package.json` 13, `package-lock.json`, `app/client/package.json` 20, `authoring/ui/package.json` (deps already by part 9: only workspace wiring here), `app/client/tsconfig.json` 15 ↔ `authoring/ui/tsconfig.json` 31, `app/client/vite.config.ts` ↔ `authoring/ui/vite.config.ts`, both `svelte.config.js`, both `index.html`, `.gitignore` + `app/client/.gitignore` + `authoring/ui/.gitignore`, `.envrc`)
   - `flake.nix`: `fromCheckout` wrappers (git root lookup, Windows irrelevant but Darwin listed in `systems` with `electron`: works?), runtime inputs actually needed per wrapper (`imagemagick`, `nodejs_22`, `claude-code`), `.#app` fileset (why `authoring/ui/package.json`), `npmDepsHash` current, devShell packages unused or missing (vs. what `README.md`/`AGENTS.md` commands need), `trivia-desktop-build` vs. D-73.
   - npm: workspaces vs. `app/desktop` and `authoring/tools` outside them (intended? lockfile per D-73?), scripts (`test --if-present`), deps declared in the wrong workspace or root, `package-lock.json` in sync (`npm ci --dry-run` offline or `npm ls`).
   - tsconfigs: strictness/flags differences, `include`/`exclude` (tests excluded from `check`: are `*.test.ts` type-checked anywhere?), `paths` vs. Vite `alias`; vite configs: proxies vs. server routes, `publicDir` sharing; `.gitignore`: stale entries (`work/`, `*.tmp`, `result-*`), untracked generated files not ignored (`git status --ignored` on a fresh build); `.envrc` `.env.local` and its "secrets" comment vs. AGENTS.md "No secrets" (inconsistency row or decision if real).
   - Check: as in "Rules"; plus `nix build .#app` and `result/bin/trivia` starts on a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` if `flake.nix` changed.
8. **Docs vs. code, and close the part** (`directory.md` 69, `AGENTS.md` 45, `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` 142; last, after tasks 1–7 and every fix of parts 2–9)
   - `directory.md`: every tracked code/config path and directory present, descriptions true after this milestone''s fixes and moves, `code-review.md` listed; `AGENTS.md`: commands exist and do what it says (`qgen report --cost`, `trivia-desktop-build`, `nix build .#app`), rules hold in the code (layout direction: grep `app/` for `authoring` imports/reads; no telemetry/network beyond decision 4); `README.md` commands and env vars run as written. Doc-only fixes here; rule changes to `AGENTS.md` → decision (plan 72 part 11 proposes process rules, don''t pre-empt).
   - Close: every part 1 row `handed to part 10` and every duplication row of parts 2–9 has a status in `## Part 10`; every file of the inventory assigned to part 10 is listed (no-findings rows included); files added since part 1 under these paths added to the inventory; remaining clusters each a follow-up task or decision.

## Done when
- Every duplication candidate of parts 2–9 and every part 1 `handed to part 10` row has a final status in `## Part 10`.
- Every part 10 inventory file (build/package config, docs check) is listed in `## Part 10`, every finding with a status.
- `directory.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` match the code.
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass (plus `nix build .#app` if the flake or lockfiles changed).', '2026-10-12T23:01:18Z', 511);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (83, 13, 'Executive summary and close-out (code review part 11)', 0, 'Part 11 of `plan 72: masterplan` (milestone 13, Code quality): close the review. Check that `code-review.md` is complete (every inventory file listed, every finding with a final status, follow-ups done or listed), propose process changes as decisions, write the executive summary at the top and run the final checks. Scope, report format and status values: plan 72 "Ground rules for every part"; not restated here.

## Depends on
- Parts 1–10 (plans 73–82), all priority 0 with lower plan ids → they and the follow-up tasks added to them run first. Tasks here read `code-review.md` and `pm` as they are then; the lists below are what the plans announced, not what they found.
- `plan 73: Baseline scans and report skeleton (code review part 1)`: the `## Inventory`, the scan commands under `## Part 1` (re-runnable), the `## Executive summary` `PLACEHOLDER(…)` this plan replaces.
- `plan 82: … (code review part 10)`: final statuses of every part 1 `handed to part 10` row and every duplication candidate; `directory.md`/`AGENTS.md`/`README.md` vs. code.
- `task 302: Delete the Python referee` (plan 51, pending decision 25): may still be open; its rows stay `superseded by task 302` and are listed as pending, not reviewed again.
- Binding: decision 14 (CI is local: per-commit checks + release check, no GitHub Actions); AGENTS.md "Outside pm workers": milestones are the gamemaster''s → process changes are `pm decision add`, never edits to `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or the milestone (plan 72 part 11).

## Rules for this plan
- No new reviews or refactors here: a gap found (file not listed, finding without status) → a short review of that file in task 1 if it fits, else `pm task add` in this plan with the exact files and the summary lists it as pending.
- Numbers in the summary come from a throw-away script over `code-review.md` and `pm` (counts per part, category, severity, status), not estimated; the script is run, not committed.
- Self-critical, factual: name the worst files/areas with row references, no praise padding; the gamemaster reads it, Spanish not needed (repo docs are English).
- `.md` style per AGENTS.md: bullets, ultra-concise; full-sentence intro paragraph allowed at the top and under each top-level heading.
- Before every commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.

## Tasks (in this order; no own priority)
1. **Completeness check of `code-review.md`**
   - Inventory vs. reality: re-run part 1''s inventory script idea against current `git ls-files` (files added, moved or deleted during the milestone, e.g. by task 302 or part 10 consolidations) → inventory rows updated (deleted → `removed (task N)`).
   - Every in-scope inventory file appears in its part''s section (finding rows or "no findings"); missing ones: short review now, or follow-up task.
   - Every row has a status from plan 72''s set; every part 1 `handed to part N` row has a final status quoted in part N''s section; every duplication candidate has a part 10 status.
   - Every `follow-up task N` / `decision N` / `superseded by task N`: `pm show` state; done tasks → status rewritten to `fixed (task N)`, dropped → `won''t fix: <reason from the drop>`; answered decisions → their follow-up''s state; still open → left, collected in a `### Pending` list under `## Part 11` (id, subject, blocking decision if any).
   - Re-run the part 1 scans whose commands are cheap (unused TS exports, markers `PLACEHOLDER`/`TODO`, bad-practice counts) → before/after counts in `## Part 11` (input for task 3); new stale `PLACEHOLDER`s → row + status.
   - Check: throw-away script prints 0 inventory files unlisted, 0 rows without valid status.
2. **Process changes as decisions**
   - From the findings (repeated categories across parts, e.g. swallowed errors, duplicated constants, stale `directory.md`, dead exports, lying comments): the systemic causes in worker-written code and what would prevent each — e.g. a rule in `AGENTS.md`, a line in pm''s worker prompt, a cheap local check added to the per-commit checks (decision 14: `tsc --noUnusedLocals`, a `directory.md` vs. `git ls-files` check, a stale-`PLACEHOLDER` check), a recurring review milestone.
   - One `pm decision add` per change (options, recommended first; body: which findings it would have prevented, cost per commit); no edits to `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, milestones or pm config. Before adding: `pm decision list --grep <term>` (open and answered) so none duplicates one.
   - Ids listed in `## Part 11` `### Process decisions` for task 3.
3. **Executive summary** (replaces the `PLACEHOLDER` under `## Executive summary` at the top)
   - Intro paragraph (full sentences): what was reviewed (files, lines, parts), when, how.
   - Before the review: overall state; systemic causes (how worker-written code drifts: per-task local view, copies instead of imports, docs not updated, tests kept by default, Python↔TS ports); worst areas with row references (files/parts with most high/medium findings).
   - Impact: counts fixed / follow-up tasks / decisions / superseded / won''t fix (per severity), notable fixes (high severity first), bundle size vs. part 1 baseline, before/after scan counts from task 1.
   - Pending: open follow-up tasks and decisions (from `### Pending`), remaining risk per area (what is unreviewed-deep, superseded, or deferred).
   - Process: the decisions of task 2 by id and one line each.
   - Length: one screen or two; details stay in the part sections.
4. **Final checks and close-out**
   - `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`; plus `nix build .#app` if any `flake.nix`/lockfile changed during the milestone (`git log` since milestone 13''s first commit).
   - Milestone 13 "Done when" walked item by item; `code-review.md` listed in `directory.md`; no `PLACEHOLDER` left in `code-review.md`.
   - Anything not met → follow-up task in this plan or a row under `### Pending`; the summary says so.

## Done when
- Every inventory file is listed and every finding has a final status; pending tasks/decisions listed.
- Process changes proposed as decisions, cited in the summary.
- Executive summary at the top of `code-review.md`, no `PLACEHOLDER` left.
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-12T23:02:07Z', 512);

