bring them in line with the plan. A task that writes a plan gets `--kind plan`.', '2026-10-12T03:44:11Z', '2026-10-12T03:44:58Z', 210);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (320, 55, 'File saves: save.mjs and main-process wiring', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/desktop/save.mjs, app/desktop/main.mjs, plans/decisions.md (D-72)', 'Part 1 of plan 55 (SW-3): the main process writes the save to one JSON file. Needs task 316 (plan 54 bridge: `preload.cjs`, origin-checked IPC in `main.mjs`); if it isn''t done, stop and say so. Follow plan 55 "Decisions taken here" (Location, Main is a dumb file store, Import).

- New `app/desktop/save.mjs` (pure `node:fs`, no Electron import): `makeSaveFile(dir, {rename = fs.rename})` → `{read(), write(text), backup(kind), dropStaleTemp()}`.
  - `read()` → text, `null` when missing.
  - `write(text)`: envelope check (≤ 10 MB, JSON object with numeric `version`) else `bad_save`; `.tmp` → write → `fd.sync()` → close → `rename` over `game.json`; `EPERM`/`EBUSY`/`EACCES` → retry 10× / 100 ms, then `save_locked`, `.tmp` removed, old file intact.
  - `backup(kind)` (`corrupt` | `newer`): rename `game.json` → `backup/game-<kind>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>.json`, `-2`, `-3` on collision; returns the path; never deletes.
  - `dropStaleTemp()`: delete a leftover `game.json.tmp`.
- `app/desktop/main.mjs`:
  - `app.setPath("userData", <appData>/trivia)` before `ready`; save dir `<userData>/save` (packaged), `<repo>/state/desktop` (dev), `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` overrides both.
  - `dropStaleTemp()` at start; IPC `save:load` / `save:write` / `save:backup` with the same origin check as plan 54; rejections carry the code.
  - One write in flight (queue); `before-quit` waits for it (`preventDefault`, then `app.quit()` again).
  - `--import-save <file>`: no `game.json` → copy in through `write()`; one exists → refuse on stderr, start normally.
- `plans/decisions.md`: next D entry (location per OS + `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`, main as dumb store / client validates, temp + backup outside the synced pattern, corrupt/newer → backup + fresh + message, import flag).

Done when (throw-away `node` script on a temp dir): read missing → `null`; write/read round trip byte-equal; injected `rename` failing `EPERM` 3× → ok, always → `save_locked` with old file byte-identical and no `.tmp`; > 10 MB, `[]`, `"x"`, no `version` → `bad_save`; two backups in the same second get distinct names; stale `.tmp` dropped, `game.json` untouched; import into an empty dir copies, with an existing save refuses and leaves it identical. `trivia-desktop` still starts. No new dependencies.', '2026-10-12T03:44:56Z', '2026-10-12T15:50:14Z', 319);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (321, 55, 'File saves: bridge, FileStore and messages', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/desktop/preload.cjs, app/client/src/lib/{desktop,store,engine}.ts, engine/save.ts (SaveNewerError), game/Game.svelte (save notice, save_locked warning), game/Overlay.svelte (flush before quit), locales/es.ts (save.*, error.save_locked); plan 55: save_locked keeps the action', 'Part 2 of plan 55 (SW-3): the client reads and writes the save through the bridge. Needs this plan''s `save.mjs` task, plan 49 task 294 (`Store`, `parseSave`, `ServerStore`) and task 298 (`lib/engine.ts`); if one isn''t done, stop and say so. Catalog keys need task 91 (LUI-1 `t()`, `es` catalog) and task 99 (`errorText` codes); if they haven''t landed, Spanish literals marked like their neighbours and a line in `plans/backlog.md`.

