- `engine/save.ts`: if `parseSave`''s error isn''t typed, add code `save_newer` for `version` > `SAVE_VERSION`.
- `lib/store.ts`: `FileStore` next to `ServerStore`, sharing its serialize/coalesce queue (extract a small helper if inline).
  - `load()`: `null` → `emptySave()`; else `parseSave(JSON.parse(text))`; on failure kind `newer` / `corrupt`, `backupSave(kind)` first, then `emptySave()` and `notice = {kind, path}`; a failed backup throws, nothing written.
  - `save()`: rejected write → `GameError("save_locked")`, in-memory save kept, next action writes the whole document again.
  - `flush()`: resolves when the queue is empty.
- `lib/engine.ts`: `desktop ? new FileStore(desktop) : new ServerStore()` (replaces plan 54''s `MemoryStore` line).
- Start screen: notice shown once (`save.corrupt` / `save.newer`, `{path}`), dismissed with `confirm` (plan 44''s action layer if landed, else Enter/click). Overlay «Salir del juego»: `await store.flush()` before `desktop.quit()`.
- `es` catalog: `save.corrupt`, `save.newer`, `error.save_locked` (texts in plan 55 "Messages").

Done when (throw-away CDP script, plan 54''s pattern, `trivia-desktop` on a temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`): new player, one answered question, «Salir» → exit 0; restart → player and burned question there, game resumes. Garbage `game.json` → backup with the original bytes, fresh save, `save.corrupt` text on screen; `version: 2` → `save.newer`; read-only `save/` → `save_locked` text, game continues, next action after `chmod u+w` writes. Browser game (`trivia`, temp `TRIVIA_STATE`) unchanged. `npm run check`, `npm run build` pass; no new dependencies.', '2026-10-12T03:44:56Z', '2026-10-12T15:58:29Z', 319);
