INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (1, 'Target count per difficulty (1–15) for 5000 approved base questions?', 'answered', '["1: 250 · 2: 350 · 3–8: 450 each · 9–11: 330 each · 12–13: 230 each · 14–15: 125 each (sum 5000)", "masterplan draft: 1–2: 490 each · 3–8: 420 each · 9–11: 300 each · 12–13: 200 each · 14–15: 100 each (sum 5000)", "flat: 333 per level (5 extra at 6–10)"]', 'Milestone 1, part 1 (D-52). Today (2026-10-11) approved base by difficulty: 1: 36 · 2: 67 · 3: 96 · 4: 104 · 5: 112 · 6: 147 · 7: 101 · 8: 67 · 9: 74 · 10: 57 · 11: 61 · 12: 38 · 13: 48 · 14: 19 · 15: 8.
The targets steer `draft` (part 2: aim at the gaps) and are the milestone''s exit check.
Recommended curve tapers at both ends; the masterplan draft puts more at 1–2 than at the middle levels, which is likely more easy questions than game nights need.', '1: 250 · 2: 350 · 3–8: 450 each · 9–11: 330 each · 12–13: 230 each · 14–15: 125 each (sum 5000)', NULL, '2026-10-11T23:16:33Z', '2026-10-12T02:09:52Z', 12, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (2, 'When is batch quality "fine": human spot-check size and agreement rate with the LLM review?', 'answered', '["30 random questions per batch; ≥ 90% agreement in each of the last two batches", "50 per batch; ≥ 95% agreement", "20 per batch; ≥ 85% agreement"]', 'Milestone 1, parts 1 and 5. After every batch the gamemaster checks a random sample in the review tool and records agree/disagree with the LLM verdict. This rate is the main "quality is fine" signal and part of the milestone''s exit check (last two batches).
30 questions take roughly 10–15 minutes; 50 gives a tighter rate but costs more of the human''s time per batch (~8 batches left).', '30 random questions per batch; ≥ 90% agreement in each of the last two batches', NULL, '2026-10-11T23:16:33Z', '2026-10-12T02:10:59Z', 12, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (3, 'How are needs_work questions (33 now, more per batch) resolved?', 'answered', '["qgen rework once after each batch''s QC, then the gamemaster decides what is still needs_work in the review tool", "the gamemaster decides all of them in the review tool; no qgen rework", "leave them; only approved questions count toward 5000"]', 'Milestone 1, part 6. RUNBOOK: `qgen rework` runs only on the gamemaster''s word; this answer is that word for the batch tasks of this milestone. batch-7 needs_work reasons: mostly giveaway hints, overlap with a pool question, or no usable media.
Rework costs LLM calls but saves the gamemaster''s time; overlaps (once part 4 drops them before merge) and media misses don''t benefit from rework.', 'qgen rework once after each batch''s QC, then the gamemaster decides what is still needs_work in the review tool', NULL, '2026-10-11T23:16:33Z', '2026-10-12T02:11:18Z', 12, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (4, 'After the engine port, which routes does the Python game server keep besides static files and /api/save?', 'answered', '["Keep /media (download on cache miss, D-17), /api/flags (state/flags.json, D-47) and /api/categories; amend the milestone''s ''static files plus /api/save only'' accordingly", "Move flags into SaveData (drop /api/flags, trivia-authoring reads game.json); keep /media and /api/categories", "Strictly static + /api/save: flags into SaveData, categories served as static files, media served only from the synced cache (no download on miss; trivia-media sync required before play)"]', 'Milestone 2 "Done when" says `trivia` serves static files plus `/api/save` only. Today `app/server/main.py` also has `/media` (cache + download on miss, D-17), `/api/flags` (game flags questions, `trivia-authoring` turns them into reviews, D-47) and `/api/categories` (all bundles, D-43). Python stays in family mode anyway (plan 12, D-3); the desktop shell (plan 18) is out of scope. Affects parts 4, 5, 6 of the masterplan.', 'Strictly static + /api/save: flags into SaveData, categories served as static files, media served only from the synced cache (no download on miss; trivia-media sync required before play)', NULL, '2026-10-11T23:56:57Z', '2026-10-12T02:50:28Z', 54, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (5, 'Where does the supply check for qgen report and the authoring start page live once app/server/selection.py has no game to serve?', 'answered', '["Move selection.py to authoring/tools/ unchanged (reads game.json), parity with engine/selection.ts guarded by the PORT-1 selection fixtures", "Authoring calls the TS engine via node (type stripping), no Python copy", "Keep app/server/selection.py where it is"]', '`qgen report` and `authoring/server/overview.py` use `selection.py` (levels, `LEVEL_RANGES`, `available`, `supply`, `burned_ids`). After PORT-8 the game no longer needs it. A Python copy duplicates the rules in two languages; calling Node from Python tooling adds a runtime hop. Plan 12 (PORT-8) left it open. Affects part 6 (and part 4''s switch of the authoring readers).', 'Authoring calls the TS engine via node (type stripping), no Python copy', NULL, '2026-10-11T23:56:58Z', '2026-10-12T02:59:57Z', 54, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (6, 'Plan 21 (LUI-1): how to check the screens show no visible change?', 'answered', '["Throw-away Playwright outside the project (nix shell / temp dir, nothing in package.json): scripted run before and after, pixel diff with ImageMagick compare", "Gamemaster clicks through by hand with a checklist the worker writes", "No screenshots: the per-task literal checks are enough"]', 'Plan 21 asks for before/after screenshots of every screen, but the flake has no headless browser and the client has no test deps. Each task already checks that every moved literal reappears verbatim in es.ts.', 'Throw-away Playwright outside the project (nix shell / temp dir, nothing in package.json): scripted run before and after, pixel diff with ImageMagick compare', NULL, '2026-10-12T00:14:30Z', '2026-10-12T02:15:40Z', 86, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 101: Task 101 (LUI-2 screen walk) reused the method: throw-away Playwright (nixpkgs python3 playwright + playwright-driver.browsers, run with LD_LIBRARY_PATH unset because the dev shell''s alsa-lib clashes with the browser''s glibc) and ImageMagick crops/montages in /tmp, nothing in the flake or package.json; temp state via TRIVIA_STATE, failures injected with page.route. Pixel diff isn''t the check for xx (it''s meant to differ): es vs xx side by side plus a DOM scan for unbracketed text and boxes past the viewport.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (7, 'Have you checked the colombia proposals at /review?bundle=colombia?', 'answered', '["checked, all moves done in the review tool", "checked, the ids to move are listed in the answer"]', 'BN-3 (qgen bundles, 2026-10-07) moved 84 existing questions to the colombia bundle; their reasons are in work/bundles/proposals.json. Rule (D-39): a question belongs in colombia only if answering needs a connection to Colombia that players outside Colombia mostly wouldn''t know. Run trivia-authoring and open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?bundle=colombia (109 questions: the 84 proposals plus later colombia questions; checking all is fine). Key n moves a question to the next bundle (colombia → base). A question moved to base needs a base subcategory (D-49); qgen validate will report it and the agent logs it for you.', 'checked, all moves done in the review tool', NULL, '2026-10-12T00:16:29Z', '2026-10-12T02:26:16Z', 90, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (8, 'Media with Commons restriction flags (personality rights, trademark, …): replace all, or let the gamemaster keep a file after checking it?', 'answered', '["Gamemaster checks each flagged file in the review tool and either keeps it (stored mark) or replaces it", "Replace every flagged file"]', 'Milestone 4 lists flagged files among those to replace; plans/17-publishing.md says the flags don''t stop editorial use in a quiz and suggests checking each file. Replacing all is simpler (no extra state) but drops usable photos of people and logos; per-file checking needs a stored ''checked, keep'' mark per slot that the audit (part 2) honours and the review tool (part 3) sets.', 'Keep every flagged file: Commons restriction flags (personality rights, trademark, …) are no reason to replace; the gamemaster has checked them, no problem in any. The audit lists the flags for information only.', NULL, '2026-10-12T00:17:48Z', '2026-10-12T03:12:56Z', 106, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (9, 'Gamepad on the Question screen: how do players pick answers and play jokers (IN-4)?', 'answered', '["Focus only: D-pad moves over the 2×2 answers and the joker tray, A locks the focused answer and focus jumps to «Respuesta final» (A again submits), B unlocks/cancels, Start = menu; LB/RB move focus into the tray (prev/next token), A arms and A again plays (today''s two-tap arming); Y = replay media; tiles keep A–D, no pad glyph on them", "Direct face buttons: Y/X/B/A pick answers by position (top-left, bottom-left, top-right, bottom-right; tiles show the pad glyph next to A–D); RT submits, LT unlocks, Start = menu; jokers by focus as in option 1", "Focus as in option 1, plus a joker wheel: holding LB opens a radial picker of the five jokers (new component), the stick picks, release plays"]', 'Plan "Gamepad input and button glyphs (IN-4, IN-5)" (masterplan 8, part 5). `plans/14-input.md` leaves this open ("To decide when designing (IN-4)").

- Recommended: option 1. Same model on every screen (navigate + A/B), no new UI, the 2×2 grid fits the D-pad, and the tray is already a column next to the answers.
- Against direct face buttons: the tiles are labelled A–D, and Xbox A/B/X/Y sit in a diamond (A bottom, B right, X left, Y top), so tile «B» would be a different pad button than B, and B would no longer mean "back" on this one screen. Speed doesn''t matter (no timer; the family discusses first).
- The wheel is the most work (new component, analog input, art) for five jokers that fit a focus column.
- Keyboard and mouse stay as today in every option.', 'Direct face buttons: Y/X/B/A pick answers by position (top-left, bottom-left, top-right, bottom-right; tiles show the pad glyph next to A–D); RT submits, LT unlocks, Start = menu; jokers by focus as in option 1', NULL, '2026-10-12T00:57:48Z', '2026-10-12T02:30:23Z', 213, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (10, 'q-0021: GFDL-only photo blocks qgen validate', 'answered', '["Gamemaster repicks q-0021''s image in the review tool (/review/q-0021); then task 113 closes", "Set q-0021 to needs_work until plan 26 part 3 replaces it", "Allowlist failures stay a validate warning until part 3; only a missing record is an error"]', 'After the licence migration (task 113), validate errors on q-0021 (approved): its media https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Container_Ship.jpg is GFDL 1.2 only, not on the allowlist (D-45). Until fixed, qgen validate and the last step of qgen batch fail. Replacements are picked by the gamemaster, not an LLM. Everything else in task 113 is done and staged.', 'Set q-0021 to needs_work until plan 26 part 3 replaces it', NULL, '2026-10-12T01:26:01Z', '2026-10-12T02:30:52Z', 113, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (11, 'Difficulty anchors 9–15: are these levels right?', 'answered', '["levels as proposed", "corrections in the answer"]', 'Proposed anchors for the house style''s calibration section (task 32 writes them in). Approved base questions, spread over 9–15 and broad categories; level = stored difficulty. Scale: 10 = 16-year-old, 12 = most adults, 14 = well-read adult / graduate in the field, 15 = trivia specialists.

- 9 · q-0023 (geografía mundo): ¿Cuál es la capital de Australia? → Canberra
- 10 · q-0833 (historia): Busto de piedra pintada hallado en 1912 en Amarna, Egipto: ¿a qué reina representa? → Nefertiti
- 11 · q-0812 (ciencia y matemáticas): Filósofo francés del siglo XVII que popularizó x, y, z para las incógnitas → René Descartes
- 12 · q-0849 (fútbol): Centrocampista española, campeona del mundo 2023, mejor jugadora del Mundial y Balón de Oro → Aitana Bonmatí
- 13 · q-1171 (inventos y tecnología): ¿Quién creó la World Wide Web y el HTML? → Tim Berners-Lee
- 13 · q-0624 (arte y literatura): Estilo de las entradas del metro de París, los carteles de Mucha y las casas de Horta → Art nouveau
- 14 · q-0814 (ciencia y matemáticas): Los siete puentes de Königsberg, imposible demostrado en 1736 → Leonhard Euler
- 14 · q-0669 (fiestas y tradiciones): ¿En cuál de estos años febrero NO tuvo día 29? → 1900
- 15 · q-0604 (Amazonas): Mariposa inofensiva que copia los colores de otra de mal sabor; el truco lleva el apellido de un naturalista inglés → Mimetismo batesiano
- 15 · q-0221 (comida y bebida): El tempura llegó a Japón hace unos 450 años desde un país europeo. ¿Cuál? → Portugal

Answer "levels as proposed", or list corrections as "q-XXXX: <level>" (and any question to drop or swap).', 'yes', NULL, '2026-10-12T01:47:40Z', '2026-10-12T02:02:22Z', 34, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (12, 'Desktop shell (OQ-29)?', 'answered', '["Electron; Steam binding: steamworks-ffi-node or steamworks.js, picked in SW-2", "Tauri v2", "Browser + local server (PyInstaller)"]', 'Shell only shows `app/client/dist/` + one save file (after milestone 2). Details: `plans/18-steam-integration.md`. Facts checked 2026-10-11.

**Facts**
- Electron: v44.7.0 (2026-10-07); zip 158 MB Win, 123 MB Linux (GitHub release assets). Same Chromium everywhere.
- steamworks.js: last npm release 0.4.0 (2024-08-06), last commit 2025-09-07, 66 open issues (GitHub API). Node-API (napi6) → not tied to an Electron version. Overlay: `electronEnableSteamOverlay()`; open issues #116 (white overlay), #160, #195 (no overlay on Linux Electron, 2025-07). → stale.
- steamworks-ffi-node: active, 0.11.3 (2026-09-24), SDK 1.64, Koffi FFI (no C++ build), experimental Electron overlay incl. Linux/SteamOS (OpenGL). Young (2025-10), 83 stars.
- Steam overlay over a system webview: no hook (tauri#6196, Construct blog "Trying to show the Steam overlay" 2023); community Win-only workaround tauri-steam-overlay-surface (2026-07).
- Tauri v2.12.3 (2026-10-10). Linux/Deck = WebKitGTK: `backdrop-filter` broken on some setups (tauri#14811, open 2026-01, NVIDIA), media via GStreamer (tauri#8579 open, #10665 AVIF), AppImage breaks on Mesa 25+ (#15665, 2026-07).
- Deck: Electron overlay is shaky on native Linux; Windows build via Proton is the common fallback. Electron bundles its engine, so either works; Tauri depends on the system WebKitGTK/WebView2.

**Phones as buzzers (OQ-37, not a blocker)**
- Electron: Node `http`/`ws`-free server in main; same TS as the client.
- Tauri: server in Rust (new language).
- Browser + local server: has one already (Python), but plans 19/20 remove Python.

**Trade-offs**
- Electron: + one engine on every target, overlay works on Win, TS only. − ~150 MB, Steam binding needs care (stale vs. young).
- Tauri: + ~10 MB. − two engines to test, our blur/video effects at risk on Deck, no overlay.
- Browser + server: + closest to today. − no game window, no overlay, two runtimes, PyInstaller AV false positives.

**Recommendation:** Electron. Wrap the Steam calls in one small bridge, so the binding can be swapped.', 'Electron; Steam binding: steamworks-ffi-node or steamworks.js, picked in SW-2', NULL, '2026-10-12T02:10:48Z', '2026-10-12T03:14:46Z', 182, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (13, 'Batch health thresholds and stop rule?', 'answered', '["Recommended set (body), stop the next qgen batch on a ✗ until qgen health ack", "Looser set (body), same stop rule", "Recommended set as warnings only: ✓/✗ in the report, no stop"]', 'Plan 15 (D-55): every batch report gets health metrics; a batch that fails a threshold makes the next `qgen batch` exit 2 until you run `qgen health ack <batch> "<note>"`. Baseline batch-4…7 (`qgen report --batches`, `authoring/reports/batches.md`; needs_work = `record`''s decisions, problems guessed from feedback for these old batches):

| metric | b4 | b5 | b6 | b7 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| drop rate (of drafts) | 1.8 % | 11.5 % | 9.9 % | 13.5 % |
| needs_work (of merged) | 7.1 % | 16.5 % | 19.5 % | 18.2 % |
| largest problem | overlap 3.6 % | media 10.6 % | giveaway 9.8 % | giveaway 8.9 % |
| overlap rate (of drafts) | 3.5 % | 3.1 % | 1.1 % | 2.7 % |
| needs_work for overlap | 3.6 % | 1.2 % | 1.2 % | 2.9 % |
| merged / slots at 11–15 | n/a | n/a | 52.5 % | 60.0 % |
| max mean-final gap to target, 11–15 | n/a | n/a | 2.0 | 2.95 |
| top move / lens | 42 / 21 % | 52 / 21 % | 15 / 21 % | 13 / 19 % |
| top clue / answer_kind | 94 / 40 % | 95 / 33 % | 43 / 44 % | 45 / 28 % |
| media share (stimulus ≠ none) | 23 % | 33 % | 26 % | 14 % |
| mean fun | 3.65 | 3.69 | 3.56 | 3.67 |
| $ per approved | $0.16* | $0.37 | $0.30 | $0.24 |

\* batch-4 without review costs. Top stimulus is 67–86 % by design (`none` weighs 7), so "top value ≤ 25 %" can''t apply to every axis.

**Recommended set** (plan''s first guess, adjusted):
- drop rate ≤ 20 %; needs_work ≤ 20 %; any one problem ≤ 10 % (was 8 %: giveaway sits at 9–10 %).
- overlap rate ≤ 3 %; needs_work for overlap ≤ 1 % (`no_overlap` in `rate` is new; b7 had 2.9 %).
- merged at 11–15 ≥ 55 % of slots there (was 60 %); mean final within ±1.5 of target at each of 11–15 (plan 13''s goal).
- top value: move and lens ≤ 25 %, answer_kind ≤ 40 %, clue ≤ 50 %; stimulus only through media share 15–50 % (was 20–50 %).
- mean fun ≥ 3.4 (new); $ per approved ≤ $0.35.
- trend: no metric worse than the mean of the previous two batches by more than half its threshold''s margin.
- batch-7 would fail 3: overlap needs_work 2.9 %, difficulty gap 2.95, media share 13.8 %. If batch-8 looks the same, batch-9 waits for your ack.

**Looser set:** drop ≤ 25 %; needs_work ≤ 25 %, one problem ≤ 12 %; overlap rate ≤ 5 %, overlap needs_work ≤ 3 %; merged 11–15 ≥ 45 %, gap ±2.5; move/lens ≤ 30 %, answer_kind ≤ 50 %, clue ≤ 60 %; media 10–60 %; fun ≥ 3.3; $ ≤ $0.50; no trend rule. batch-7 passes all.

**Warnings only:** the recommended numbers, ✓/✗ in the reports and `batches.md`, but `qgen batch` never stops.', 'Recommended set (body) without the trend rule; a ✗ stops the next qgen batch until qgen health ack. Trends stay visible in batches.md only.', NULL, '2026-10-12T02:40:28Z', '2026-10-12T03:18:52Z', 45, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (14, 'CI builds (SW-6): in S3 or S5, and with or without media?', 'answered', '["Move SW-6 to S5; local builds only in S3 (the gamemaster''s machine has the media)", "Keep SW-6 in S3: GitHub Actions builds both artefacts without media (smoke test; media added locally or as its own depot in S5)", "Keep SW-6 in S3: GitHub Actions fetches the media with trivia-media sync (cached between runs)"]', '- S3 builds nothing for upload; the local command (plan "Local builds for Windows and Linux") makes both artefacts on Linux (Windows as a zip, no wine needed).
- Media is gitignored (D-17): CI has none unless it downloads ~720 MB from Commons and others per cache miss (rate limits, flaky, needs Python + Nix in CI).
- A no-media CI build only proves the code packages; the packaged game shows the missing-media notice on every media question.
- S5 needs CI or a local upload anyway (plan 18 "Builds and depots": media as a shared content depot, upload by hand is the documented alternative).
- Recommended: move to S5, where the upload and the depot split decide what CI must build.', 'No GitHub Actions. CI is local: the pm workers'' per-commit checks (npm run check, npm test, npm run build, qgen validate, the task''s own check; made explicit in AGENTS.md) plus a release check command (e.g. trivia-release-check) run before every Steam upload: the per-commit checks, trivia-media licenses, the release quality bar (decision 15), nix build .#app and the packaged Linux/Windows builds, a short scripted smoke game in the packaged build (CDP), and a manual checklist (start test on clean Windows and the Deck, sound, the timed-competitive red frame). Steam upload by hand with steamcmd in S5. SW-6 redefined accordingly.', NULL, '2026-10-12T03:46:55Z', '2026-10-12T16:54:52Z', 211, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 333: 2026-10-12, task 333: SW-6 redefined as local CI and moved to S5 (11-steam S3 row SW-1..SW-5, S5 row SW-6..SW-14); per-commit checks (npm run check, npm test, npm run build, qgen validate, task check) as a rule in AGENTS.md; D-73 gains a CI line; plan 18 ''Builds and depots'' lists the release check (S5), no GitHub Actions secrets, upload by hand with SteamCMD; B-11 no longer relies on CI; the release check command is owned by plan 10 part 7 (task 261); no .github/workflows.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (15, 'Release quality bar (CT-5): D-56''s numbers or stricter for the Steam release?', 'answered', '["Stricter: D-56''s agreement plus at most 2 false approves in the 30 and none of kind fact; batch or slice above it → full audit + gamemaster decides flagged + second spot check", "D-56''s numbers only (>= 90 % agreement, last two batches); a batch below it only feeds QC step 4 (prompt changes), no full audit", "Strictest: spot check 50 per batch for release, at most 1 false approve and none of kind fact; same consequence as option 1"]', 'Plan ''Release quality bar and back-audit (CT-5)'' (milestone 9). D-56/pm decision 2 measure agreement only: 30 spot-checked per batch, >= 90 % human/LLM agreement in the last two batches; a disagreement can be a false needs_work (harmless) as well as a false approve (a wrong or weak question on the TV). For buyers, false approves and wrong facts are what count. batch-7 baseline: audit found a major problem in 9/49 (18 %) LLM-approved questions (mostly giveaways). ''Above the limit'' = the batch or back-audit slice is not release-ready: every approved question of it gets the LLM audit (not only the sample of 60), the gamemaster decides the flagged ones in /review?audit=flagged, then a second spot check (new seed) of 30; release-ready once that passes. Family play is not affected (statuses stay as the gamemaster decides).', 'D-56''s numbers only (>= 90 % agreement, last two batches); a batch below it only feeds QC step 4 (prompt changes), no full audit', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:02:14Z', '2026-10-12T16:57:56Z', 241, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (16, 'Back-audit: start the pilot slice (100 oldest approved questions, ~$5 opus)?', 'answered', '["start the pilot slice once the tooling is done", "not now: drop the back-audit (old pool stays unaudited for release)"]', 'Plan 57 ''Release quality bar and back-audit (CT-5)''. 1136 questions approved before D-56 never had an LLM audit or spot check. Pilot slice: qgen audit --backlog --slice 100 (pilot + start of first-120), one opus call per question (batch-7 baseline ~$0.046/question), then a blind spot check of 30 in /review?run=backaudit-1&sample=1 (~15 min of the gamemaster) and qgen report --qc. The pool is never changed by the audit. After the pilot, a second decision asks whether to run the remaining ~1000 (~$45).', 'start the pilot slice once the tooling is done', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:03:37Z', '2026-10-12T16:58:58Z', 335, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (17, 'Run the next qgen rework with --model fable (~$14+, plan 58)?', 'answered', '["yes, run the next rework with Fable once the flag exists", "not now: keep rework on opus", "drop the experiment (flag stays, unused)"]', 'Plan 58 ''Fable as an opt-in model for qgen rework''. qgen rework runs only on the gamemaster''s word. rework-1 (opus): 43 questions, 54 calls, $5.57. Fable 5.1 is 2.5x per token plus thinking → roughly $14+ for a similar run; whether it shares Opus''s subscription limit is unknown (check /usage before and after). Fix and review 1 run on Fable, fact check stays sonnet, review 2 stays opus so the verdict is comparable. Result: approval rate, cost per approved question, then a keep/drop/extend decision.', 'yes, run the next rework with Fable once the flag exists', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:12:11Z', '2026-10-12T17:01:41Z', 343, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (18, 'Which new base subcategories?', 'answered', '["add the recommended ones", "add all", "none for now"]', '20 proposals for new `base` subcategories (plan 14, task 38), from `qgen report --subcategories` on 2026-10-11 (batch-6, batch-7). ★ = recommended (15). Task 39 adds the approved ones to `app/data/categories.json` and creates their concept lists. No new broad categories; names checked against `base` and `colombia` (D-43); no Colombia-only topic (D-49). Sample concepts: name (known_at).

## Source (a): saturated subcategories
- Report flags 4 of 184: Plantas del Amazonas, Caballeros, Villanos famosos (overlaps 2/10, 2/15, 2/17), Productos del supermercado (8 unused hard).
- The 3 overlap flags are cross-subcategory near-synonyms (Caballeros/Castillos, …): plan 15''s job; lists still have 121–184 unused. No split recommended for them.

1. ★ **Historia de los alimentos** (Comida y bebida). Where foods come from and how they spread: Columbian exchange, spice routes, first recipes. Reason: hard neighbour for Productos del supermercado (8 hard) and Origen de las marcas (15 hard). Samples: Papa de los Andes (5), Chocolate azteca (7), Ruta de las especias (10), Intercambio colombino (12), Garum romano (14), Pasteurización (11), Tomate en Europa (9), Ketchup de salsa de pescado china (13), Café de Etiopía (8), Azúcar y esclavitud en el Caribe (12).
2. **Samuráis y ninjas** (Historia). Feudal Japan''s warriors, weapons, code, famous figures. Reason: neighbour for Caballeros (overlaps 2/15); Historia already has 18 subcategories, hence not recommended. Samples: Katana (4), Ninja (3), Shogun (9), Bushido (11), Seppuku (12), Miyamoto Musashi (13), Los 47 rōnin (13), Tokugawa Ieyasu (14), Armadura samurái (6), Shuriken (5).

## Source (b): broad categories with ≤ 3 subcategories
- Espacio 1 (11 approved), Cuerpo humano 2 (11; 36 unused hard, thinnest), Fiestas y tradiciones 2, Fútbol 2, Videojuegos 3 (51 unused hard), Amazonas 3.
- At 5000 with today''s split: Espacio ~27 questions, Cuerpo humano / Fútbol / Fiestas ~54, Historia ~490 (D-53).

3. ★ **Sistema solar** (Espacio). Sun, planets, moons, dwarf planets, comets. Reason: Espacio has 1 subcategory; split out of its 255-concept list. Samples: Saturno (2), Luna (1), Marte (3), Júpiter (4), Plutón planeta enano (7), Cinturón de asteroides (8), Gran Mancha Roja (10), Europa luna de Júpiter (12), Nube de Oort (13), Titán y sus lagos de metano (14).
4. ★ **Carrera espacial y astronautas** (Espacio). Missions, rockets, astronauts, space agencies, space stations. Reason: Espacio balance. Samples: Neil Armstrong (5), Apolo 11 (6), Laika (8), Yuri Gagarin (9), Sputnik (10), Valentina Tereshkova (12), Apolo 13 (11), Wernher von Braun (13), Programa Vostok (14), Baikonur (13).
5. ★ **Estrellas y galaxias** (Espacio). Stars, constellations, nebulae, black holes, telescopes, astronomers. Reason: Espacio balance; hard-heavy. Samples: Estrella fugaz (2), Vía Láctea (5), Osa Mayor (6), Agujero negro (8), Telescopio Hubble (10), Año luz (9), Casiopea (11), Andrómeda (11), Supernova (12), Enana blanca (13), Tycho Brahe (14).
6. ★ **Medicina y salud** (Cuerpo humano). Diseases, vaccines, medicines, history of medicine, famous doctors. Reason: Cuerpo humano has 2 subcategories and the fewest unused hard (36). Samples: Vacuna (3), Estetoscopio (5), Penicilina (8), Rayos X (7), Hipócrates (11), Alexander Fleming (10), Peste negra (9), Edward Jenner y la viruela (12), Ignaz Semmelweis (14), Insulina (12).
7. ★ **Cerebro y mente** (Cuerpo humano). Brain, nerves, sleep, memory, reflexes, senses in the brain. Reason: Cuerpo humano balance, hard supply. Samples: Cerebro (1), Sueño (2), Reflejo (5), Neurona (8), Memoria a corto plazo (9), Fase REM (11), Hemisferios cerebrales (10), Hipocampo (13), Sinapsis (12), Phineas Gage (15).
8. **Genética y ADN** (Cuerpo humano). DNA, genes, heredity, twins, blood groups. Reason: Cuerpo humano balance; overlaps a bit with Ciencia, hence not recommended. Samples: Gemelos (2), Grupo sanguíneo (6), ADN (7), Gen (8), Cromosoma (10), Gregor Mendel (11), Doble hélice (12), Oveja Dolly (11), Rosalind Franklin (14), Proyecto Genoma Humano (13).
9. ★ **Calendarios y Año Nuevo** (Fiestas y tradiciones). Calendars, leap years, zodiacs, New Year customs worldwide. Reason: Fiestas y tradiciones has 2 subcategories. Samples: Uvas de Nochevieja (4), Año bisiesto (6), Horóscopo chino (7), Año Nuevo chino (6), Calendario maya (10), Calendario gregoriano (11), Calendario juliano (12), Nowruz (13), Rosh Hashaná (13), Ramadán y calendario lunar (11).
10. **Halloween y fiestas de muertos** (Fiestas y tradiciones). Halloween, Día de Muertos, Obon, Samhain and their symbols. Reason: Fiestas balance; much of it is easy, and Celebraciones del mundo covers some, hence not recommended. Samples: Calabaza de Halloween (1), Truco o trato (2), Catrina (6), Pan de muerto (7), Ofrenda (8), Jack-o''-lantern (9), Samhain (12), Obon japonés (13), Cempasúchil (11), Todos los Santos (6).
11. ★ **Modales y costumbres del mundo** (Fiestas y tradiciones). Greetings, table manners, gestures, gifts, taboos around the world. Reason: Fiestas balance; rich in hard «which country» questions. Samples: Dar la mano (2), Reverencia japonesa (6), Propina (7), Palillos clavados en el arroz (10), Siesta (5), Beso en la mejilla (4), Namasté (9), Mano izquierda en India (11), Meishi tarjetas japonesas (13), Hongi maorí (14).
12. ★ **Clubes de fútbol del mundo** (Fútbol). Big clubs outside Colombia, their nicknames, stadiums, rivalries. Reason: Fútbol has 2 subcategories; world clubs only (Colombian clubs live in `colombia`). Samples: Real Madrid (3), FC Barcelona (3), Boca Juniors (6), Santiago Bernabéu (7), El Clásico (8), Ajax (10), Superclásico (10), Old Firm (13), Los Colchoneros (12), Estadio Maracaná (9).
13. ★ **Futbolistas legendarios** (Fútbol). Great players of all eras outside Colombia, their records and nicknames. Reason: Fútbol balance. Samples: Messi (2), Cristiano Ronaldo (2), Pelé (5), Maradona (6), Mano de Dios (9), Zidane (8), Johan Cruyff (11), Lev Yashin (13), Ferenc Puskás (13), Alfredo Di Stéfano (12).
14. **Copas y torneos de fútbol** (Fútbol). Champions League, Copa América, Libertadores, Euro, Balón de Oro. Reason: Fútbol balance; close to Mundiales de fútbol, hence not recommended. Samples: Champions League (4), Copa América (5), Balón de Oro (6), Eurocopa (7), Copa Libertadores (8), Copa Africana (11), Recopa (12), Grecia Euro 2004 (12), Bota de Oro (10), Copa Intercontinental (13).
15. ★ **Consolas y empresas de videojuegos** (Videojuegos). Consoles, handhelds, makers, history of the industry. Reason: Videojuegos has 3 subcategories and 51 unused hard. Samples: PlayStation (2), Nintendo Switch (2), Game Boy (5), Atari (8), Sega (7), Xbox (4), Nintendo fundada con naipes (11), Dreamcast (12), Magnavox Odyssey (14), Ralph Baer (14).
16. **Esports y juegos en línea** (Videojuegos). Online games, esports, streaming, tournaments. Reason: Videojuegos balance; ages fast, hence not recommended. Samples: Fortnite (2), Minecraft multijugador (3), Twitch (6), League of Legends (8), Counter-Strike (9), The International (12), Faker (13), MMORPG (11), World of Warcraft (9), Speedrun (10).
17. ★ **Historia y exploración del Amazonas** (Amazonas). Explorers, legends of El Dorado, rubber boom, Amazon cities. Reason: Amazonas has 3 subcategories, and it gives Plantas del Amazonas (overlap flag) a neighbour. Samples: Río Amazonas (2), Manaos (8), El Dorado (7), Francisco de Orellana (11), Amazonas guerreras mitológicas (9), Fiebre del caucho (12), Teatro Amazonas (13), Fordlandia (14), Percy Fawcett (14), Encuentro de las Aguas (12).

## Source (c): topics with hard questions (11–15)
18. ★ **Rocas, minerales y gemas** (Planeta Tierra). Rocks, minerals, gemstones, fossils formation, Mohs scale. Reason: Planeta Tierra subcategory has 13 unused hard; adult-school knowledge. Samples: Diamante (2), Oro (2), Esmeralda (5), Cuarzo (8), Mármol (7), Roca volcánica (6), Escala de Mohs (12), Obsidiana (11), Roca sedimentaria (10), Feldespato (14).
19. ★ **Economía y bolsa** (Monedas y dinero). Inflation, markets, crashes, famous economists, trade. Reason: hard topic adults know and children don''t; Monedas y dinero has 4 subcategories. Samples: Oferta y demanda (8), Inflación (9), Wall Street (8), Crac de 1929 (11), Adam Smith (12), PIB (11), Tulipomanía (13), Keynes (14), Burbuja puntocom (13), Hiperinflación de Weimar (14).
20. **Arquitectos famosos** (Arquitectura y monumentos). Architects and their signature buildings. Reason: hard topic; overlaps Estilos arquitectónicos and Monumentos famosos, hence not recommended. Samples: Gaudí (8), Sagrada Familia (6), Gustave Eiffel (7), Le Corbusier (12), Frank Lloyd Wright (12), Zaha Hadid (12), Oscar Niemeyer (13), Frank Gehry y Guggenheim Bilbao (11), Brunelleschi (13), Mies van der Rohe (14).', 'The recommended (★) set minus 12 (Clubes de fútbol del mundo) and 13 (Futbolistas legendarios); instead add «Historia del fútbol» and «Fútbol internacional» (Fútbol), kept at general-knowledge level, not fan-specific (football-centric detail is too specific for base). 15 new subcategories in total.', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:14:44Z', '2026-10-12T17:06:08Z', 38, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (19, 'Default mode: presets, checkpoints and won levels (OQ-30)?', 'answered', '["Draft table as is, 4 presets, Normal default; presets set only the joker budget (difficulty = age group); no checkpoint; only level 12 = won, the level reached is kept per game for stats/achievements later", "As 1, plus on Fácil a checkpoint at level 6 as a safe mark: losing from level 6 on is shown and stored as a partial result («¡Mitad del camino!»); no replay, no extra burns", "As 1, plus on Fácil a fall-back checkpoint: one wrong answer above level 6 per game drops back to level 6 with fresh cards (up to ~6 extra burns); only 12 = won", "As 1, but presets also shift difficulty: Fácil −1, Difícil/Experto +1 on every level range, clamped to the group''s window (plan 28 tunes 16 tables)"]', 'Plan 35 / MD-5. Default mode = one team, no gamemaster (plans/13-game-modes.md). Age group (D-38, plan 27: 12 level ranges per group in age-groups.json `levels`, tuned in plan 28) is a separate setting either way.

Facts
- Burns (D-28, per player): every answered question, plus each Paso, Bájale, Cambiazo and Snipe hit (the replaced card). Soplo and Snipe misses burn nothing (a miss still uses the joker, MD-2).
- Max burns per won game with the draft table: Fácil 24 (Soplo ∞ is free), Normal 20 (= «Como las cartas», JK-11), Difícil 16, Experto 12. A lost game burns fewer. Input for OQ-32 / plan 38.
- Presets shifting difficulty = 4 groups × 4 presets = 16 range tables, plan 28 tunes 4; Difícil/Experto upward hits the thin top (adults level 12: 27 candidates). The age group already is the difficulty knob.
- Checkpoint as fall-back (wrong answer above level 6 → back to 6): game continues, so a game can take > 12 answers (breaks "12 to victory" as a clean count); each fall-back burns up to +6 and redraws the thin upper levels. Needs a cap (once per game).
- Checkpoint as safe mark (Millionaire style): wrong answer still ends the game, but reaching 6 is recorded as a partial result. No extra burns.
- Today the game row stores result won/lost/abandoned; the level reached is in the state, so "highest level" stats need no new data.

Draft presets (Soplo/Paso/Bájale/Cambiazo/Francotirador): Fácil ∞/3/3/3/3, Normal 4/2/2/2/2, Difícil 2/1/1/1/1, Experto 0/0/0/0/0.', 'None of the options: there is no default mode (milestone 7, Game modes). «Alone or as group» has no difficulty presets and no difficulty selection: the player picks the age group, and one standard joker set applies to every age group. Customization only via a small "Customize game" button on the age group screen; only uncustomized games earn Steam achievements. No checkpoint.', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:24:25Z', '2026-10-12T16:32:59Z', 184, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 248: No preset or per-mode content targets: plan 70 (CT-3/CT-4) aims generation only at D-75''s per-level mix; the simulation uses the one standard joker set.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (20, 'Default mode: which admin actions in the Esc menu (OQ-30)?', 'answered', '["Esc menu: «Reportar pregunta» (burn for everyone here, report list, replacement; the replacement once per game, later reports only log and the question stays), «Abandonar partida», sound. No undo, no «Saltar y quemar para todos», no budget change, no pause", "As 1, but every report replaces the question (no limit; trust the player)", "As 1, but a report never replaces: it logs, and the question is burned for everyone after the game; the player answers or uses a joker"]', 'Plan 35 / MD-5; MD-6 builds «Reportar pregunta», MD-7 the settings screen. Gamemaster mode keeps its overlay as is (D-30).

Facts
- Gamemaster overlay today: «Saltar y quemar para todos», undo, «Abandonar partida», sound, joker budget for this game (MD-4).
- Without a gamemaster, undo and a free skip are cheat buttons; a mid-game budget change bypasses the preset.
- «Reportar pregunta» (plan 13 draft): burn the question for everyone on this machine (player NULL, D-28), add it to a local report list (a page to copy from), draw a replacement. With unlimited replacements it is a free Paso; cheating only costs the player''s own pool, but matters once Steam achievements exist.
- No timer (OQ-4), so no pause is needed; the screen just waits.', 'Option 3, stricter: outside gamemaster mode a question can never be skipped, not even a broken or far too hard one. «Reportar pregunta» only logs (no replacement); the player answers or uses a joker. No undo, no free skip, no joker changes mid-game; abandon and sound stay. Gamemaster mode has its own full cheat menu (milestone 7).', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:24:33Z', '2026-10-12T16:32:59Z', 184, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (21, 'Content target per player and language (OQ-32)?', 'answered', '["≥ 50 games per new player in the primary language (Spanish), ≥ 30 in every other launch language; solo, Normal preset, strong-player bound, every age group; D-52''s 5000 meets it (~80, adults'' top); CT-2 (S4) verifies", "≥ 30 games per new player in every launch language (same bound); 5000 base exceeds it, a ~1900-question pool would meet it; CT-2 (S4) verifies", "A target per age group: ≥ 50 for kids and young_teens, ≥ 30 for young_adults and adults (thin hard top accepted); CT-2 (S4) verifies", "No games number: D-52''s 5000 with D-53''s mix per launch language is the target; CT-2 (S4) reports games per player for information"]', 'Plan 38 / CT-1. Games per new player before questions repeat, per launch language. Estimate only; CT-2 (`qgen report --simulate`, S4) verifies or corrects the number. Throw-away script, deleted.

Facts
- Approved `base` today (questions.json, 2026-10-11): 1034. Per difficulty 1–15: 36, 67, 96, 103, 112, 147, 101, 67, 74, 57, 61, 38, 48, 19, 8.
- Target: D-52 5000; D-53 per difficulty (targets.json, pm decision 1 answered): 250, 350, 450×6, 330×3, 230×2, 125×2.
- Draw (D-22, D-27, D-28, D-31): 4 cards shown per level, ≥ 1 burned per ladder level; level ranges per age group from age-groups.json (D-38; only young_teens tuned, AG-7).
- Burns per won game: 12 without jokers; Normal preset draft 12 + Paso 2 + Bájale 2 + Cambiazo 2 + Snipe hits 2 = 20 (pm decision 19 open, draft used). Assumed worst case: the 8 joker burns land on levels 9–12. Presets don''t shift the window (decision 19 draft option 1).
- Launch languages: OQ-31 open (plan 37) → draft "Spanish only". A translation counts as a full pool only once its own approved pool meets the target.
- Extra players: OQ-37 open (plan 41) → target is for solo play; burn multiplier per extra player named open.

Estimate (strong-player bound, solo; min over ladder levels of approved in the level''s range ÷ burns there; also checked on shared difficulty intervals, which is tighter where levels overlap)
- Today, Normal: adults 9 (bottleneck level 12, difficulty 14–15: 27 q); young_adults 21 (levels 9–12, difficulty 9–13); kids 33, young_teens 33 (level 1, difficulty 1: 36 q, and 8–10).
- Today, no jokers: adults 27, kids/teens 36, young_adults 56.
- At 5000 (D-53 mix), Normal: adults 80 (difficulty 13–15), young_adults 112, kids 129, young_teens 155. No jokers: ≥ 239 everywhere.
- Bottleneck: the top of adults (difficulty 14–15, 125 each at target). Scaling D-53''s mix: ≥ 30 games needs ~1900 approved, ≥ 50 ~3100.
- Not in the estimate: subcategory depth for Bájale/Cambiazo, category spread; CT-2 covers them.

Quality bar: D-56 and pm decision 2 (30 spot-checked per batch, ≥ 90 % agreement); release bar pm decision 15. No new numbers.

Trade-offs
- 50/30: met by 5000 `base` with margin (80); a second language needs ~1900 approved of its own.
- 30 everywhere: same 5000 already exceeds it; sets a lower bar for later languages and for a smaller early pool, but buyers notice repeats sooner.
- Per age group: allows thin adult tops, but the store can''t say one number.', 'No games number: D-52''s 5000 with D-53''s mix per launch language is the target; CT-2 (S4) reports games per player for information', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:38:20Z', '2026-10-12T16:42:58Z', 191, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 248: Plan 70: per-locale deficits use targets.json base''s numbers for es, en, de (no locale block); simulation bottlenecks don''t feed draft weights; budget sized from the deficit to 5000 per language.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (22, 'Approve the age-group windows', 'answered', '["approve the proposal", "keep the draft windows", "adjust (name the change)"]', 'AG-7, plan 28. Measured 2026-10-11 on 1136 approved questions (`base` 1034, `colombia` 102); full tables, weights and demand in `plans/21-age-groups.md`, "Measured windows (AG-7)". `young_teens` stays D-22 (window 1–10).

Proposal (`{base}`; thinnest level by candidates; games one player can play until a level runs dry, median of 20 seeds; `{base, colombia}` in brackets):
- `kids` 1–7 → **1–6**: 1, 2, 2–3, 2–4, 3–4 ×2, 3–5, 4–5 ×2, 4–6, 5–6 ×2. Thinnest L1 (1) 36 → 36. Until dry 9 → 9 ([9 → 9]). Draft top 6–7 = a 13-year-old, too hard for 10-year-olds.
- `young_adults` 3–13 → **4–13**: 4, 5–6, 6–8, 7–9 ×3, 8–10, 9–11, 9–12, 10–13, 11–13 ×2. Thinnest L12 (12–13) 86 → L1 (4) 103. Until dry 10 → 10 ([11 → 11]).
- `adults` 4–15 → **5–15**: 5, 6–7, 7–9, 8–10 ×2, 8–11, 9–11, 10–12, 10–13, 11–14, 12–15, 13–15. Thinnest L12 (14–15) 27 → L12 (13–15) 75. Until dry 4.5 → 8 ([5 → 9]).
- `young_teens` (D-22): thinnest L1 (1) 36, until dry 9 ([9]).
- Every level ≥ 36 candidates; overlap kept (5–6 serve all four groups).
- `level_weights` per group derived from the ranges; `young_teens` = `qgen.LEVEL_WEIGHTS`.

Thin top, for milestone 1 (not fixed here): difficulty 14: 19 approved, 15: 8. Adults'' top levels run dry first even widened; `young_adults`'' 11–13 (147) after 10 games.

Answer is applied by task 127.', 'approve the proposal', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:41:04Z', '2026-10-12T16:39:24Z', 126, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (23, 'Competitive format (OQ-37)?', 'answered', '["Relay ladder on one shared tower, turns in fixed order; each player 1 joker per game (any kind); no attack jokers; per-player windows for mixed age groups; burns 12+(N−1)+N per won game (≈1× solo Normal); shell: nothing", "As 1, but one window for the game (the youngest player''s)", "As 1, but each player gets the chosen preset''s budget (pm decision 19); burns 12+(N−1)+8N (4 adults today: 1 game)", "Parallel ladders: own tower per player, one level per round, all see all; burns 12N–20N", "Buzzer round: everyone sees the question, first to buzz answers, points per round; ~12 burns per round; needs one pad per player or phones"]', 'Plan 41 / MD-8. Several players, no gamemaster, one screen. Input is the second decision («Multiplayer input and couch co-op (OQ-37)»).

Facts (no web in this run: sources from memory, re-check in task 202)
- Burning (D-28): every question shown burns for every player in the game, so a regular group burns the union of what it saw.
- Comparable games: Jackbox Trivia Murder Party / You Don''t Know Jack (phones, 1–8, everyone answers in parallel; jackboxgames.com); Trivial Pursuit Live! (Ubisoft, Steam, 1–4 local, pads/hot-seat; store page); Buzz! (PlayStation, 4–8 USB buzzers; not on Steam). Buzzers need one device per player (decision 2).
- Win rule (relay): wrong answer knocks that player out; the next player gets a new card on the same level; last player in wins (may play on to 12).

Burns per won game (solo: 12, Normal preset 20, pm decision 19 draft)
- Relay, 1 joker per player: 12 + (N−1) + N → 2: 15, 4: 19, 8: 27 (≈ 1× Normal solo).
- Relay, preset per player (Normal 8 burns each): 12 + (N−1) + 8N → 4: 47, 8: 75.
- Parallel ladders: 12N (no jokers) to 20N.
- Buzzer: 12 per round (no jokers), more rounds per game.

Games a regular group can play until a level runs dry (strong players, draft windows, approved `base` 1034 today → at 5000 D-53 mix; throw-away sim, median of seeds)
- adults: solo Normal 6 → 52; relay 1 joker N=4 9 → 76, N=8 4 → 38; relay preset N=4 1 → 17; parallel N=4 4 → 38.
- young_teens: solo Normal 22 → 115; relay 1 joker N=4 29 → 151, N=8 16 → 84; relay preset N=4 7 → 38; parallel N=4 9 → 62.
- → relay with 1 joker each lasts as long as solo Normal; preset-per-player and parallel ladders burn 3–5× faster.

Mixed age groups (D-38, D-68: age group is per game today)
- One window (youngest''s): adults win easily; no engine change.
- Per-player windows: each turn draws from the player''s group range for that level (handicap, like family editions of board trivia); supply check per group present; `settings.age_group` becomes per player in this mode.

Attack jokers («give the next player a harder card»): new joker kind, art, rules, more burns; recommended no (later idea).

Shell needs (plan 34): none for relay/parallel; buzzer needs one pad per player (≤ 4) or the phone server.', 'None of the options as is; four modes besides gamemaster mode (milestone 7, Game modes): «Alone or as group»; round-robin co-op (turns, one team, one age group, shared jokers); round-robin competitive (turns, each player their own game, own jokers, own age group); competitive timed (own tracks, 30 s per answer, a hint every 8 s, no jokers, one age group, question difficulty = average of all players progress, wrong answer = out, three levels behind = out, first to level 12 wins; timeout rule still to decide).', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:43:51Z', '2026-10-12T16:32:59Z', 201, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 248: Plan 70: no per-mode targets; mode bottlenecks from qgen report --simulate are information for the gamemaster and the budget decision.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (24, 'Multiplayer input and couch co-op (OQ-37)?', 'answered', '["Hot-seat for competitive (any input acts for the player on turn); no separate couch co-op (any pad drives the default mode); no phones (IN-7: no); IN-6 = ''every connected pad acts'' only, no join screen; Remote Play Together works as is; shell: nothing", "As 1, plus one pad per player (≤ 4) with a «Pulsa A para unirte» join screen; couch co-op team confirm by majority", "As 2, but couch co-op confirm by one captain pad", "Phones as buzzers (LAN server in Electron, QR join, firewall prompt), own later task; hot-seat stays as the fallback"]', 'Plan 41 / IN-6, IN-7, MD-9. Format: pm decision 23. Shell is Electron (D-63).

Facts (no web in this run: sources from memory, re-check in task 202)
- Gamepad API in Chromium/Electron: `navigator.getGamepads()` has 4 slots (Chromium `Gamepads::kItemsLengthCap`); XInput on Windows also 4 (`XUSER_MAX_COUNT`, Microsoft docs).
- Steam Input turns most pads into virtual Xbox pads; the Deck''s controls are pad 1, external pads add more (plan 14 §2, Steamworks Steam Input docs).
- Remote Play Together: friends join via the Steam overlay; their pads (and, if the host allows, keyboard/mouse) arrive as input on the host; up to 4 players, more on fast connections (store.steampowered.com/remoteplay). Works with hot-seat too: any remote pad can press for the player on turn. Needs only an opt-in in Steamworks (SW-13).
- Phones as buzzers: Jackbox uses its own internet servers (jackbox.tv room code), not LAN. Here: Node `http` + WebSocket in Electron''s main process, QR with the LAN address, Windows Defender firewall prompt on first listen, some guest Wi-Fis block client-to-client; weakens "offline, one machine"; a page to build and test on phones.
- Default mode is already a team game: the family discusses, one person presses (as with the gamemaster today).

Options per part
- Couch co-op: (a) no separate mode: the default mode, any pad/mouse/keyboard drives the one focus; (b) a pad per player and a team confirm (majority / captain): join screen, vote UI, more rules for 1× burn.
- Competitive input: (a) hot-seat: «Turno de Ana», any input acts for the player on turn, no join screen; (b) one pad per player (≤ 4, more players share): join screen + binding (IN-6); needed only for a buzzer format; (c) phones: up to 8+, own later task.
- Burns: input doesn''t change burns (co-op = 1× solo).

Shell needs (plan 34): (a) nothing beyond the Gamepad API; (b) nothing; (c) LAN server + firewall prompt in Electron main.', 'Gamepads (one per player), keyboard and mouse; no phones. Plus a shared keyboard: every player has one dedicated key; pressing it gives that player keyboard and mouse until their turn is done. Timed competitive: everyone answers at once, each with their own input.', NULL, '2026-10-12T04:44:02Z', '2026-10-12T16:32:59Z', 201, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (25, 'Family test night on the TS engine', 'pending', '["test night played fine", "problems (listed in the answer)"]', 'The game now runs its referee in the browser (TypeScript engine, plan 50, D-69). Before the Python game routes are deleted (plan 51), please play one family test night on it.

What changes for you:
- First `trivia` start after pulling migrates the save: `state/game.sqlite` (+ `state/flags.json`) → `state/game.json`. The terminal prints a migration line. `game.sqlite` and `flags.json` stay as backups; from then on only `game.json` is written.
- After `qgen export`, reload the game page (F5): the pool is loaded once per page load.
- Rollback: stop `trivia`, delete `state/game.json`, `git checkout 7788cb3` (the commit before the switch, task 298 = c345e90), start `trivia`.
- No browser check was done by an agent (no browser tool); a node check on a copy of the real save passed in task 298.

Checklist:
- [ ] Players list shows the family; the running game (if any) continues
- [ ] A full game to level 12
- [ ] Every joker: hint, skip, skip+purge, easier, category, snipe (animations show)
- [ ] A wrong answer
- [ ] Admin overlay: undo, abandon, joker budget
- [ ] Flag a question, see it in `trivia-authoring`
- [ ] Delete a (test) player

Answer "problems" with one line per problem.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-12T04:50:41Z', NULL, 299, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (26, 'Launch languages (OQ-31): which languages at Steam launch, and which comes first after?', 'answered', '["Spanish only at launch; English named as the first post-launch language (plan 24 stays as later work)", "Spanish only; no later language planned (plan 24 to be dropped by the gamemaster)", "Spanish + English at launch (plan 24 and QT-6 become S4 work)", "Spanish + English + more at launch (name them)"]', 'Plan 37, I18N-1. Today: everything Spanish (D-6); the pipeline, review and family checks are Spanish. Also decides whether plan 24''s `en` catalog is launch or later work.

Facts
- Steam survey language shares (approx., from memory of 2025 surveys; web lookup unavailable, gamemaster to confirm at store.steampowered.com/hwsurvey): English ~35–40 %, Simplified Chinese ~25–50 % (swings monthly), Russian ~9 %, Spanish – Spain ~4–5 %, Portuguese – Brazil ~3–4 %, German ~3 %, Spanish – Latin America ~1–2 %. Steam lists "Spanish – Spain" and "Spanish – Latin America" as separate store languages.
- Pool: 1,136 approved (base 1,034, colombia 102) of 1,211 (`authoring/data/questions.json`, 2026-10-12).
- Cost per approved question (generation + fix + review): $183 / 835 approved = ~$0.22 (batches 4–7, `work/*/costs.log`). Translation proxy (translate + re-rate + fact-check + review, 15b): ~$0.10–0.22. × plan 16 draft 2,000–3,000 → ~$200–650 per language, plus a native speaker''s review time (the real bottleneck).
- UI: `app/client/src/locales/es.ts` 218 lines, ~126 keys (LUI-1 done); one more UI language is small (15a, LUI-3 draft exists as plan 24).

Trade-offs
- Spanish only: Spanish shares ~5–7 % of Steam; every review stays with the family. OQ-32: one target. D-50: only «Trivia en Familia» + English store name.
- + English: biggest share, ~$200–650 + native review of 2,000–3,000 questions; English trivia market is crowded; difficulty re-rated per locale. OQ-32: two targets. D-50: English name «Living Room Trivia» becomes an in-game name too.
- More (pt-BR, de …): cost × N, no native reviewer in the family.', 'Spanish, English and German at launch. Later languages: Simplified Chinese, Russian, Portuguese (Brazil) in milestone "Conquer the world" (12), on hold.', NULL, '2026-10-12T05:30:16Z', '2026-10-12T16:46:09Z', 189, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 248: Plan 70: cost projection, deficits and release budget per es, en, de; en/de deficits filled through --translate from es sources, with es source shortfall feeding draft once es meets 5000.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (27, 'Spanish variety (OQ-31): which Spanish does base speak, and which Steam store languages to tick?', 'answered', '["Neutral Latin American Spanish in base (rewrite ~40 Colombianisms via the pipeline, S4), Colombian in colombia; tick Spanish – Latin America and Spanish – Spain", "Keep Colombian usage as is; tick Spanish – Latin America and Spanish – Spain", "Keep Colombian usage as is; tick Spanish – Latin America only", "Neutral base + per-variety variants (es-419 and es-ES)"]', 'Plan 37, I18N-1. D-6: Colombian usage where natural. D-39/D-49: `colombia` bundle holds what needs a real Colombian connection, `base` the rest. D-50 picked «Trivia en Familia» partly because «sala»/«salón» splits Spanish.

Facts
- Pool: base 1,034 approved / 1,102; colombia 102 / 109 (`authoring/data/questions.json`, 2026-10-12).
- Colombian vocabulary in approved base (throw-away regex over question, answers, hints, fun fact): 40 / 1,034 (~4 %) with a clear Colombianism (computador(es) 25, bombillo(s) 14, crispetas 3, banano(s) 4, arequipe, guayabo, cobija …). Pan-LatAm forms common: carro(s) ~40, celular(es) 22; «ustedes» not «vosotros» (1 hit, 0 «vosotros»). Reads as Latin American, not regional.
- Steam store languages: "Spanish – Latin America" and "Spanish – Spain" separate; Spain''s share is ~2–4× LatAm''s (approx., see the launch-languages decision).

Trade-offs
- As is, tick LatAm + Spain: no work; Spain players see LatAm forms (carro, celular, ustedes) — understandable, common in Steam games. OQ-32: one Spanish target.
- Neutral LatAm in base, Colombianisms only in colombia: rewrite ~40 base questions through the pipeline (S4 backlog row, D-36), prompts say neutral LatAm from then on; cheap. OQ-32: one target. D-50 unchanged.
- Neutral + per-variety variants (es-419 / es-ES): two text sets per question, double review; OQ-32: shared target, variants per question. D-50: maybe two Spanish names.
- LatAm only: drops the larger Spanish store audience for no saving.', 'Two variants: base in neutral Latin American Spanish (es-419; rewrite the ~40 Colombianisms via the pipeline), plus an es-ES variant only where the wording differs (regionalisms, vosotros in the UI). The colombia bundle keeps its Colombian voice. Tick Spanish – Latin America and Spanish – Spain. No finer variants; regional flavour comes from bundles (later e.g. mexico, argentina).', NULL, '2026-10-12T05:30:29Z', '2026-10-12T16:48:57Z', 189, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (28, 'Steam binding for the Electron shell?', 'answered', '["steamworks-ffi-node: maintained, current SDK, documented electron-builder setup; overlay experimental (OSR)", "steamworks.js: bigger user base, libs bundled; unmaintained since 2024-08, open overlay/asar bugs", "Decide in S5 (SW-8) after a spike with both on the Deck"]', 'Facts checked 2026-10-12. Used in the main process only (no Node in the page). Both MIT, both N-API (ABI-stable, so Electron 43 loads them; neither names 43). Needed for SW-8 (overlay, achievements, on-screen keyboard, language); no dependency added in S3.
- steamworks-ffi-node (github.com/ArtyProf/steamworks-ffi-node): 0.11.3 on 2026-09-24, monthly releases, 19 open issues, 83 stars. Loads via `koffi` FFI (+ small `steam-overlay.node` prebuilds); Steamworks SDK 1.64 `redistributable_bin` supplied by us (Valve licence), path set by `setSdkPath`. electron-builder: documented `asarUnpack` for the package, `koffi`, `@koromix/koffi-*`, `steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin`. Overlay: "experimental, working": renders the window offscreen (OSR) into a native OpenGL window Steam hooks; tested Windows, Deck desktop mode; X11 only, no Wayland; ~50–100 MB, one frame latency; untested with our video/audio.
- steamworks.js (github.com/ceifa/steamworks.js): npm 0.4.0 on 2024-08-06 (no release since), last commit 2025-09-07, 66 open issues, 635 stars. napi-rs prebuilds with `steam_api64.dll`/`libsteam_api.so` inside the package (win64, linux64, osx); built against Electron 24. Overlay: `electronEnableSteamOverlay()` (in-process-gpu, per-frame invalidation); open issues: Linux overlay (#195, 2025), white overlay (#116), video tag breaks overlay (#148), asar (#153), forge binaries (#75).
- Either way the Deck/Linux overlay is a risk; fallback stays the Windows build via Proton (D-63, SW-12).', 'steamworks-ffi-node: maintained, current SDK, documented electron-builder setup; overlay experimental (OSR)', NULL, '2026-10-12T14:42:40Z', '2026-10-12T17:07:55Z', 317, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (29, 'Desktop shell plays?', 'pending', '["plays fine", "problems (listed)"]', 'SW-2 (plan 54, D-71). `npm run build -w app/client && trivia-desktop`: play a short game with sound, F11 toggles fullscreen, ☰ → «Salir del juego» quits. Save stays in memory until SW-3. Automated check passed 2026-10-12: whole game to level 12 under Xvfb, every joker, undo, abandon, all media loaded, samples decoded, console clean, no Python.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-12T15:48:35Z', NULL, 318, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (30, 'Start milestone "Conquer the world" (zh, ru, pt-BR)?', 'answered', '["start now"]', 'The milestone is on hold: its masterplan task waits for this decision. Answer when the launch languages (en, es, de) are far enough along.', 'Replaced by the milestone hold: milestone 12 is on hold (pm milestone hold 12); resume it with pm milestone resume 12 when the launch languages are far enough along.', NULL, '2026-10-12T16:46:08Z', '2026-10-12T17:25:38Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (31, 'Low-supply warning: below how many fresh games left (K) should the game start warn?', 'answered', '["3", "2", "5"]', 'Plan 65 replaces burning with seen counters. At game start the engine computes k = how many more games the profile can play with only unseen questions (per mode, bundles, age group). The start screen shows an informational warning («Quedan preguntas nuevas para unas 2 partidas; …», «Jugar» stays) when k < K. k = 0 shows «En esta partida pueden salir preguntas que ya vieron.»

- 3 (plan proposal): a few nights of notice before repeats start.
- 2: fewer warnings; notice only shortly before.
- 5: early notice, more often shown.', 'Super tight, no K: warn only when a difficulty level the planned session needs (mode, bundles, age group) has 1 or 0 unseen questions left. Why not earlier: a repeated question does no immediate harm. General rule: every information or warning about running out of questions uses this super-tight criterion, not an early-notice threshold.', NULL, '2026-10-12T18:26:35Z', '2026-10-12T18:43:52Z', 418, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (32, 'Neutral Spanish prompts for base (plan 64)', 'answered', '["approve as drafted, numbers RAE style (2640, 42 195, 42,195)", "approve as drafted, but keep Colombian numbers (2.640, 42,195)", "changes: …"]', 'Plan 64 task 1 (task 430), D-78: `base` in neutral Latin American Spanish (es-419), `colombia` stays Colombian. New prompts are the gamemaster''s (D-36), so the live prompts are unchanged until you answer; every `qgen batch` reads them. Tasks 431 (`qgen neutralize`) and 432 (docs) wait for this decision.

## Size of the problem (base, 1102 questions, any text field)
- bombillo 10, crispetas 5, gripa 4, arquero 11, tinto 6, pelotica 2, computador 13; carro 29, celular 27 (no pan-Hispanic form).

## Voice mechanism (code, applied in the second pass)
- New field `voice` per bundle in `app/data/bundles.json` (English, for prompts, like `rule`).
- `prompt()` fills `{voices}` in house-style.md with every bundle''s voice ("- `base`: …", "- `colombia`: …"), like `{players}`.
- Why all bundles and not just the batch''s: review, audit, rework, tighten and back-audit runs mix bundles under one system prompt. So each question''s `bundle` goes into the per-question input of rate, revise, review and audit (review and audit inputs lack it today); the drafter''s "## Bundle" section (`bundle_text`) adds that bundle''s voice.
- New regional bundles (RG-3..RG-5) just add their own `voice`.

## Number format (options 1 and 2)
- Today "the Colombian way": 2.640 / 42,195. Not pan-Hispanic: Mexico and Central America write 2,640 / 42.195, so "42.195" can read as 42 thousand or 42 point.
- Option 1 (recommended, in the drafts): RAE/ISO style for all bundles: "2640", "42 195", decimal comma "42,195 km", large round numbers in words. No dot/comma clash; RAE''s own recommendation. The neutralize scan also flags dotted thousands in `base`.
- Option 2: keep "2.640 / 42,195" (Colombia, Argentina, Chile, Spain…); the house-style line stays as today and the scan''s number bullet is dropped.

## es-ES for questions (recommendation, no file at launch)
- No `questions.es-ES.json` at launch: neutral wording reads fine in Spain.
- The neutralize scan returns `no_neutral_form` (carro/coche, celular/móvil…); if many, a sparse es-ES override can follow (backlog, not this plan).
- The UI''s es-ES (`vosotros`) stays LUI-5.

## Other changes in the drafts
- House-style examples: "pelotica" → "pelota"; description example labels "Chigüiro"/"Bombillo" → English labels (the Spanish example sentences are unchanged).
- review.md new reason 8, problem kind `style`; audit.md check 7 extended. No schema change.
- neutralize.md: scan prompt like tighten.md (output per question `id` + `issue`; `no_neutral_form` is a new list in the scan schema, task 431).

## Diffs
```diff
--- a/authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md
@@ -8,9 +8,11 @@
 {players}
 
 ## Language
-- All content is in Spanish, with Colombian usage: "bombillo", "carro", "celular", "gripa", "crispetas", "arquero", "tinto" (black coffee), "parcero" only in jokes.
-- Use Colombian references where they fit naturally (places, food, music, sport, people, Encanto), but don''t force them. Each batch writes for one bundle (D-41): a `base` question may use Colombian references anyone in the Spanish-speaking world knows, but never needs a connection to Colombia to answer; that is the `colombia` bundle''s job.
-- Write numbers the Colombian way: "2.640 metros", "42,195 km".
+- All content is in Spanish. The voice depends on the question''s bundle:
+{voices}
+- Neutral means: a word understood across Latin America and in Spain where one exists ("bombilla", "palomitas", "gripe", "portero", "café"); no regional diminutives ("pelota", not "pelotica"); "tú", never "vos" or "vosotros". Where no word is shared ("carro"/"coche"/"auto", "celular"/"móvil"), reword around it if that stays natural ("vehículo", "teléfono"); else take the most widespread Latin American form.
+- Use Colombian references where they fit naturally (places, food, music, sport, people, Encanto), but don''t force them. Each batch writes for one bundle (D-41): a `base` question may use Colombian references anyone in the Spanish-speaking world knows, but never needs a connection to Colombia to answer; that is the `colombia` bundle''s job. A neutral voice is about the words, not the topics.
+- Numbers (all bundles): no thousands separator up to 9999 ("2640 metros"), a space from 10 000 ("42 195 personas"), a decimal comma ("42,195 km"); large round numbers in words ("3 millones").
 
 ## Format: multiple choice
 - Exactly one correct `answer` and exactly three `wrong_answers`. The game shuffles them.
@@ -23,7 +25,7 @@
 - The same goes for "¿Cuál de estas ciudades está a mayor altura?": ask "¿Cuál es la capital departamental más alta de Colombia?" instead.
 - The clue in the question must point to the answer **in the real world**, not just among the four options. Before writing, ask: "What else in the world fits this clue?" If anything does, use a clue that only the answer has.
